## Construction and escalation

Step 1 keeps existing drift/source recovery, readiness, scope, page-capacity and
owner-hold mechanisms. Initial authors use `gpt-6-luna-max`; drift/source recovery
retains its existing model assignments. Both drift reviewers and authors
must escalate significant unmet prerequisites directly to the owner, giving the
smallest missing supplier, consuming claims/steps and affected consumers.
Scaffolding agents fully author all assigned items, pages and proof contracts;
a proof strategy or successful process alone is not a completed carrier.
Readiness records bind the finished carriers. Initial authoring fills every
available worker slot, up to the shared cap of 30, taking lower dependency levels
first across the complete pending queue. Levels are priorities, not completion
barriers: authors start and continue even when another pair's supplier is missing.
As soon as a worker finishes, the engine starts the next pending pair without
waiting for the rest of its level.

Batch levels are computed mechanically during planning, recomputed after drift
materialization and at the drained construction join, and recorded in
`research/RUN-batch-dependency-levels.json`. Queue refill and status use that last
valid full graph while authors edit draft manifests and carrier YAML. The loader
validates its DAG, levels and complete current manifest batch scope without
parsing in-flight drafts. The drained join and gates strictly recompute and check
the current graph, including declared carrier dependencies. No
cross-pair prerequisite-completion barrier applies to initial authoring. A missing
supplier retains its exact planned interface and honest proof-status obligation;
authors complete the consuming argument conditionally and continue their remaining
work. They keep explicit unresolved readiness records, never invent supplier
acceptance or duplicate another pair's ownership. Completion accounting requires
local authored carriers, inventories, contracts, coverage and readiness records.
The complete, drained Step-1 gate battery still requires current supplier content,
resolved readiness and correct dependency levels before review. This adds no stage.

Per-item Step-1 readiness recording retains the complete manifest page/pair and
item ownership index, but hashes only the target and its actual transitive
dependencies, including explicitly examined context. A bare item ID in an
unrelated unfinished inventory does not prevent that local authoring record;
the same unfinished ID in the target's dependency closure fails recording.
Unrelated malformed carrier YAML is deferred during identity/alias indexing;
a reached carrier is parsed strictly, and relevant duplicate identity or alias
claims remain blocking. Malformed JSON, ambiguous ownership and invalid
page/pair structure still fail.
The hash calculation and alias resolution are shared with the strict full-frontier
checker; local readiness records grant no global acceptance or gate authority.

At a drained owner join, `recordStep1Batch(root, {run, records, owner: true})`
from `tools/physics-support/step1-decisions.mjs` can record multiple independently
reviewed readiness dispositions without rebuilding the full alias index per item.
Each record supplies the ordinary `item`, `decision`, `reason` and explicit
`dependencies` fields. The owner preserves prior rows before replacement and
supplies actual scientific evidence; batching grants no review or gate authority.
All records and ownership are validated before any writes. One shared local
snapshot hashes each actual dependency closure plus examined context; a second
fresh snapshot must reproduce every hash before the native-format rows are
written. Relevant mutation aborts the batch without writing rows; unrelated
unfinished drafts retain the ordinary local-recording exclusion. Keep writers
drained through recording. The individual `record` CLI remains unchanged.

Item `dependency_level` is determined before writing item/page carriers, recorded
and independently checked in Step 1: zero
without in-run logical suppliers, otherwise one plus the maximum supplier level.
External suppliers remain context. No rebatching or additional agent stage
is introduced. Logical dependencies must agree between authored bodies and
manifests; aliases resolve to canonical suppliers. Definition discharges and
nonlogical links are hash-bound context, not extra logical scheduling edges.

`node tools/physics-support/depcheck.mjs --help` (or `-h`) prints usage and
budget; duplicate pending requests retain the same label. Only an engine-started,
matching fresh successful native result discharges the request. Coverage masks that
unit until then, including after restart; siblings keep their coverage. Actual
artifacts and the complete ordinary Step-1 battery remain required. A second
continuation for the same unit is refused, and an unresolved result escalates to
the owner. Closed stages cannot be reopened by this command. The CLI only writes a
control request; upgrading controller code and supervising restart/resume remain
owner operations.

## Cross-batch dependency inputs

Each batch writes `research/RUN-batch-N.cross-batch-dependencies.json` as an
array, including an empty array when it has no declared in-run cross-batch
edges. The collector derives edges from current manifest and source `requires`
for pages, and `deps`, `justified_by`, and `forward_refs` for items. Reviews use
one row per exact consumer/supplier edge:

```json
[
  {
    "kind": "item",
    "consumer": "lem-example-consumer",
    "supplier": "def-example-supplier",
    "status": "open",
    "evidence": "Exact declared dependency; the scoped supplier-use check remains pending."
  }
]
```

`kind` is `item` or `page`, and the consumer must belong to the batch writing
the file. `status` is `open`, `verified`, or `removed`, with nonempty evidence.
// Current frontier inventories and hash-bound prerequisite inputs; no review decisions.
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';
import { existsSync, readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { yaml } from './pathway-lib.mjs';
import { parseFrontmatter } from './content-policy-lib.mjs';
const safe = value => { if (!/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/.test(value ?? '')) throw Error('Invalid identity'); return value; };
const json = path => JSON.parse(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));
const read = path => existsSync(path) ? json(path) : null;
const hash = value => createHash('sha256').update(JSON.stringify(value)).digest('hex');
export function loadStep3(root, run) {
  safe(run);
  const dir = join(root, 'research'), pages = [], items = new Map(), pairs = new Map();
  for (const f of readdirSync(dir).filter(f => new RegExp(`^${run}-batch-\\d+\\.pages\\.json$`).test(f)).sort()) {
    const batch = f.match(/-batch-(\d+)\./)[1];
    const coverage = read(join(dir, f.replace('.pages.json', '.coverage.json')));
    for (const page of json(join(dir, f))) {
      const livePage = { ...page, batch, coverage: coverage?.pages?.find(p => p.page === page.id) };
      pages.push(livePage);
      for (const item of page.items ?? []) {
        if (items.has(item.id)) throw Error(`Duplicate item ${item.id}`);
        items.set(item.id, { item, page: livePage });
      }
    }
  }
  if (!pages.length) throw Error('No run manifests');
  const claimedCompanions = new Set();
  for (const a of pages.filter(p => p.kind === 'A')) {
    const b = pages.find(p => p.id === a.companion && p.kind === 'B');
    // The plan contract names companions on A pages; B pages may omit the
    // reverse pointer. Reject a contradictory pointer or a shared B page.
    if (!b || (b.companion && b.companion !== a.id) || pairs.has(a.id)
      || claimedCompanions.has(b.id)) throw Error(`Invalid pair ${a.id}`);
    claimedCompanions.add(b.id);
    pairs.set(a.id, [a, b]);
  }
  if (pairs.size * 2 !== pages.length) throw Error('Every page must belong to one A/B pair');
  const planned = new Map();
  for (const page of read(join(dir, 'plan-spec.json'))?.pages ?? [])
    for (const item of page.items ?? []) planned.set(item.id, { item, page });
  return { root, run, pages, pairs, items, planned, cache: new Map() };
}

// Recording authoring readiness is local; global review/gates still use loadStep3.
// Keep the complete ownership index, including unfinished bare-ID inventories,
// but reject an unfinished entry if it actually enters the recorded closure.
export function loadStep1Record(root, run) {
  safe(run);
  const dir = join(root, 'research'), pages = [], items = new Map(), pairs = new Map();
  const invalidItems = new Map(), homes = new Set();
  const files = readdirSync(dir).filter(f => f.startsWith(`${run}-batch-`) && f.endsWith('.pages.json')
    && /^\d+$/.test(f.slice(`${run}-batch-`.length, -'.pages.json'.length))).sort();
  for (const f of files) {
    const batch = f.slice(`${run}-batch-`.length, -'.pages.json'.length);
    const manifest = json(join(dir, f));
    if (!Array.isArray(manifest) || !manifest.length) throw Error(`Invalid run manifest ${f}`);
    for (const page of manifest) {
      if (!page || typeof page !== 'object' || typeof page.id !== 'string' || !page.id
        || homes.has(page.id) || !['A', 'B'].includes(page.kind)
        || !Array.isArray(page.items) || !Array.isArray(page.requires ?? [])
        || (page.requires ?? []).some(id => typeof id !== 'string' || !id))
        throw Error(`Invalid or ambiguous page ownership in ${f}`);
      homes.add(page.id);
      const livePage = { ...page, batch };
      pages.push(livePage);
      for (const item of page.items) {
        const id = typeof item === 'string' ? item : item?.id;
        safe(id);
        if (items.has(id)) throw Error(`Duplicate item ${id}`);
        items.set(id, { item, page: livePage });
        if (typeof item === 'string') invalidItems.set(id, `Unfinished manifest inventory for ${id} in ${f}`);
      }
    }
  }
  if (!pages.length) throw Error('No run manifests');
  const claimedCompanions = new Set();
  for (const a of pages.filter(p => p.kind === 'A')) {
    const b = pages.find(p => p.id === a.companion && p.kind === 'B');
    if (!b || (b.companion && b.companion !== a.id) || pairs.has(a.id) || claimedCompanions.has(b.id))
      throw Error(`Invalid pair ${a.id}`);
    claimedCompanions.add(b.id);
    pairs.set(a.id, [a, b]);
  }
  if (pairs.size * 2 !== pages.length) throw Error('Every page must belong to one A/B pair');
  const planned = new Map();
  for (const page of read(join(dir, 'plan-spec.json'))?.pages ?? [])
    for (const item of page.items ?? []) planned.set(item.id, { item, page });
  return { root, run, pages, pairs, items, planned, invalidItems, cache: new Map() };
}

// Proof repairs do not reopen scope. Changed claims or inventory do.
export function scopeHash(s, page) {
  const pair = s.pairs.get(page);
  if (!pair) throw Error(`Unknown A page ${page}`);
  return hash(pair.map(p => ({ id: p.id, title: p.title, category: p.category,
    items: p.items.map(i => ({ id: i.id, kind: i.kind, title: i.title, statement: i.statement })),
  })));
}

function dependency(s, id) {
  if (s.invalidItems?.has(id)) throw Error(s.invalidItems.get(id));
  if (s.cache.has(id)) return s.cache.get(id);
  const live = s.items.get(id), planned = s.planned.get(id);
  const path = join(s.root, 'items', `${safe(id)}.md`);
  const body = existsSync(path) ? readFileSync(path, 'utf8') : null;
  const fm = body ? parseFrontmatter(body.match(/^---\r?\n([\s\S]*?)\r?\n---/)?.[1] ?? '') : null;
  if (fm && fm.id !== id) throw Error(`Invalid authored identity ${id}: ${fm.id}`);
  const contract = live ?? planned;
  // Missing prerequisites must remain auditable and escalatable, not prevent dispatch.
  if (!contract && !fm) return { bytes: { missing: id }, deps: [] };
  const declarations = [contract?.item, fm].filter(Boolean);
  if (s.invalidItems) for (const declaration of declarations) {
    for (const field of ['deps', 'justified_by', 'forward_refs', 'aliases']) {
      const values = declaration[field] ?? [];
      if (!Array.isArray(values) || values.some(value => typeof value !== 'string' || !value))
        throw Error(`${id}: ${field} must name dependency IDs`);
    }
  }
  const { verification, ...mathematicalMetadata } = fm ?? {};
  const value = {
    bytes: [contract?.item ?? null, body === null ? null : [mathematicalMetadata,
      body.replace(/^---\r?\n[\s\S]*?\r?\n---/, '')],
      contract ? { id: contract.page.id, order: contract.page.order, requires: contract.page.requires } : null],
    deps: [...new Set(declarations.flatMap(i => [...(i.deps ?? []), ...(i.justified_by ?? []), ...(i.forward_refs ?? [])]))],
  };
  s.cache.set(id, value);
  return value;
}

// Like the physics repository loader, defer unrelated carrier parse errors.
// Recover only identity claims from the renderer's YAML document nodes, never
// metadata used for hashing. A reached carrier is parsed strictly by dependency.
function localIdentity(s, token) {
  if (!s.identityIndex) {
    const ids = new Map(), aliases = new Map();
    const add = (map, key, name) => {
      if (typeof key !== 'string' || !key) return;
      if (!map.has(key)) map.set(key, new Set());
      map.get(key).add(name);
    };
    for (const name of readdirSync(join(s.root, 'items')).filter(name => name.endsWith('.md'))) {
      const id = name.slice(0, -3);
      add(ids, id, id);
      const text = readFileSync(join(s.root, 'items', name), 'utf8');
      const doc = yaml().parseDocument(text.match(/^---\r?\n([\s\S]*?)\r?\n---/)?.[1] ?? '');
      // Valid YAML aliases/anchors have exactly the ordinary parser meaning.
      if (!doc.errors.length) {
        try {
          const fm = doc.toJS();
          if (Array.isArray(fm?.aliases)) for (const alias of fm.aliases) add(aliases, alias, id);
        } catch {
          // Unresolved YAML anchors can fail conversion without parse errors.
          // Retain raw identity claims below; reached content is still strict.
        }
      }
      // Inspect all claims (including duplicate YAML keys), so malformed YAML
      // cannot hide an alias collision or a second claim to a reached identity.
      if (yaml().isMap(doc.contents)) for (const pair of doc.contents.items) {
        if (!yaml().isScalar(pair.key)) continue;
        if (pair.key.value === 'id' && yaml().isScalar(pair.value)) add(ids, pair.value.value, id);
        if (pair.key.value === 'aliases') {
          if (yaml().isSeq(pair.value)) {
            for (const alias of pair.value.items) if (yaml().isScalar(alias)) add(aliases, alias.value, id);
          } else if (yaml().isScalar(pair.value)) add(aliases, pair.value.value, id);
        }
      }
    }
    s.identityIndex = { ids, aliases };
  }
  const { ids, aliases } = s.identityIndex;
  const matches = ids.get(token) ?? aliases.get(token);
  if (matches?.size > 1) throw Error(`Ambiguous prerequisite identity or alias ${token}`);
  return matches?.values().next().value ?? token;
}

function itemInputs(s, id, extra = []) {
  if (!s.items.has(id)) throw Error(`Unknown run item ${id}`);
  if (!Array.isArray(extra) || extra.some(d => typeof d !== 'string')) throw Error('dependencies must be an ID array');
  const seen = new Map(), queue = [id, ...extra];
  while (queue.length) {
    let key = queue.pop();
    if (s.invalidItems) key = localIdentity(s, key);
    else if (!s.items.has(key) && !s.planned.has(key) && !existsSync(join(s.root,'items',`${safe(key)}.md`))) {
      if (!s.aliases) {
        s.aliases=new Map();
        const names=readdirSync(join(s.root,'items')).filter(name=>name.endsWith('.md'));
        const canonical=new Set(names.map(name=>name.slice(0,-3)));
        for(const name of names){
          const text=readFileSync(join(s.root,'items',name),'utf8');
          const fm=yaml().parse(text.match(/^---\r?\n([\s\S]*?)\r?\n---/)?.[1]??'')??{};
          for(const alias of fm.aliases??[])if(!canonical.has(alias)){
            if(s.aliases.has(alias)&&s.aliases.get(alias)!==name.slice(0,-3))throw Error(`Ambiguous alias ${alias}`);
            s.aliases.set(alias,name.slice(0,-3));
          }
        }
      }
      key=s.aliases.get(key)??key;
    }
    if (seen.has(key)) continue;
    const node = dependency(s, key);
    seen.set(key, node.bytes);
    queue.push(...node.deps);
  }
  return seen;
}

export function itemHash(s, id, extra = []) {
  return hash([...itemInputs(s, id, extra)].sort(([a], [b]) => a.localeCompare(b)));
}

// Use the same transitive closure as itemHash when checking who authored its
// current inputs. Both item text and run/planned dependency metadata contribute.
export function itemInputPaths(s, id, extra = []) {
  const paths = new Set();
  for (const key of itemInputs(s, id, extra).keys()) {
    const itemPath = join(s.root, 'items', `${safe(key)}.md`);
    if (existsSync(itemPath)) paths.add(itemPath);
    const live = s.items.get(key);
    if (live) paths.add(join(s.root, 'research', `${s.run}-batch-${live.page.batch}.pages.json`));
    else if (s.planned.has(key)) paths.add(join(s.root, 'research', 'plan-spec.json'));
import { realpathSync as physicsRealpath } from 'node:fs';
// Scaffold readiness records; no dispatches, repairs, or proof approvals.
import { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';
import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';
import { loadStep3, loadStep1Record, itemHash } from './frontier-snapshot.mjs';

const safe = value => {
  if (!/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/.test(value ?? '')) throw Error('Invalid run or item ID');
  return value;
};
const file = (root, run, id) => join(root, 'research', `${safe(run)}-step1-${safe(id)}.json`);

export function step1Decision(s, id) {
  const path = file(s.root, s.run, id);
  if (!existsSync(path)) return { closed: false, reason: 'Readiness record missing' };
  const row = JSON.parse(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));
  if (row.version !== 1 || row.run !== s.run || row.item !== id
      || !['ready', 'escalated'].includes(row.decision) || typeof row.owner !== 'boolean'
      || !row.reason?.trim() || !Array.isArray(row.dependencies)) throw Error(`Invalid Step 1 record: ${id}`);
  if (row.decision === 'escalated') return { closed: false, owner: true, row, reason: row.reason };
  if (row.sha256 !== itemHash(s, id, row.dependencies))
    return { closed: false, owner: row.owner, row, reason: 'Item or dependency changed; record current readiness' };
  return { closed: true, row };
}

export function checkStep1(s) {
  const work = [];
  for (const id of s.items.keys()) {
    const result = step1Decision(s, id);
    if (!result.closed) work.push({ item: id, page: s.items.get(id).page.id, ...result });
  }
  for (const page of s.pages) if (!page.items?.length)
    work.push({ page: page.id, reason: 'Empty scaffold inventory' });
  return { run: s.run, items: s.items.size, ready: s.items.size - work.filter(x => x.item).length,
    closed: work.length === 0, work };
}

function validateRecord({ run, item, decision, reason, dependencies, owner = false }) {
  safe(run); safe(item);
  if (!['ready', 'escalated'].includes(decision)) throw Error('Decision must be ready or escalated');
  if (typeof reason !== 'string' || !reason.trim()) throw Error('Record evidence or the exact blocker');
  if (!Array.isArray(dependencies) || dependencies.some(d => typeof d !== 'string' || !d.trim()))
    throw Error('Record examined dependency IDs, including an explicit empty list');
  if (typeof owner !== 'boolean') throw Error('Owner must be a boolean');
}

function buildRecord(s, { run, item, decision, reason, dependencies, owner = false }) {
  if (!s.items.has(item)) throw Error(`Unknown run item ${item}`);
  if (s.invalidItems.has(item)) throw Error(s.invalidItems.get(item));
  const previous = step1Decision(s, item);
  if (!owner && (previous.owner || previous.row?.owner)) throw Error('Only the owner may resolve this record');
  if (previous.closed && !owner) throw Error('Keep unchanged ready items and records intact');
  return { version: 1, run, item, decision, owner, reason,
    dependencies: [...new Set(dependencies)].sort(), sha256: itemHash(s, item, dependencies),
    at: new Date().toISOString() };
}

function writeRecord(root, row) {
  writeFileSync(file(root, row.run, row.item), JSON.stringify(row, null, 2) + '\n');
}

export function recordStep1(root, options) {
  validateRecord(options);
  const row = buildRecord(loadStep1Record(root, options.run), options);
  writeRecord(root, row);
  return row;
}

/** Owner-only drained readiness recording. This shares snapshot caches, never
 * scientific dispositions. Validate the whole batch and recapture its actual
 * input closures before writing any native-format rows. */
export function recordStep1Batch(root, { run, records, owner }) {
  if (owner !== true) throw Error('Only the owner may record a readiness batch');
  safe(run);
  if (!Array.isArray(records) || !records.length) throw Error('Readiness batch must be nonempty');
  const seen = new Set();
  const options = records.map(record => {
    if (!record || typeof record !== 'object' || Array.isArray(record)) throw Error('Invalid readiness batch record');
    if (record.run !== undefined && record.run !== run) throw Error('Readiness batch run mismatch');
    if (record.owner !== undefined && record.owner !== true) throw Error('Readiness batch records are owner-only');
    const value = { ...record, run, owner: true };
    validateRecord(value);
    if (seen.has(value.item)) throw Error(`Duplicate readiness batch item ${value.item}`);
    seen.add(value.item);
    return value;
  });
  const s = loadStep1Record(root, run);
  const rows = options.map(record => buildRecord(s, record));
  // No prior snapshot cache may mask an edit made while the first was captured.
  // Rebuilding also rechecks complete manifest ownership and relevant aliases.
  const fresh = loadStep1Record(root, run);
  for (const row of rows) {
    const current = buildRecord(fresh, row);
    if (current.sha256 !== row.sha256) throw Error(`Readiness batch inputs changed during capture: ${row.item}`);
  }
  for (const row of rows) writeRecord(root, row);
  return rows;
}

if (process.argv[1] && import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(physicsRealpath(resolve(process.argv[1]))).href) {
  try {
    const args = process.argv.slice(2), get = key => {
      const at = args.indexOf(`--${key}`);
      return at < 0 ? undefined : args[at + 1];
    };
    if (args[0] === 'check') {
      const result = checkStep1(loadStep3(process.cwd(), get('run')));
      console.log(JSON.stringify(result, null, 2));
      process.exitCode = result.closed ? 0 : 1;
    } else if (args[0] === 'record') {
      console.log(JSON.stringify(recordStep1(process.cwd(), { run: get('run'), item: get('item'),
        decision: get('decision'), reason: get('reason'), owner: args.includes('--owner'),
        dependencies: get('dependencies') === undefined ? undefined : JSON.parse(get('dependencies')),
      }), null, 2));
    } else throw Error('Usage: step1-decisions.mjs check --run RUN; record --run RUN --item ID --decision ready|escalated --dependencies JSON --reason TEXT [--owner]');
  } catch (error) { console.error(error.message); process.exitCode = 1; }
}

