  "statement": "Assume the axiom of countable choice. Let\n$G=SU(2)=\\{U\\in M_2(\\mathbb C):U^*U=I_2,\\ \\det U=1\\}$ with its real Lie-group\nstructure. Define the Pauli matrices\n$\\sigma_1=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix}$,\n$\\sigma_2=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\\\i&0\\end{pmatrix}$, and\n$\\sigma_3=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}$, and put\n$T_a=-\\frac{i}{2}\\sigma_a$ for $a\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$. Then $G$ is compact and\nnoncommutative, its real Lie algebra has basis $T_1,T_2,T_3$ with\n$[T_a,T_b]=\\sum_{c=1}^3\\epsilon_{abc}T_c$, and the real bilinear form\n$\\kappa(X,Y)=-2\\operatorname{Tr}_2(XY)$ on $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ is positive\ndefinite, symmetric, and invariant under\n$\\operatorname{Ad}_gX=gXg^{-1}$, with $\\kappa(T_a,T_b)=\\delta_{ab}$.",
  "definition": null
}
{
  "id": "post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model",
  "kind": "postulate",
  "dependency_level": 2,
  "deps": [
    "def-qft-framework-units",
    "def-gauge-group-of-a-smooth-principal-bundle",
    "def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data",
    "def-qftx-principal-connection-form",
    "def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket",
    "lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi",
    "def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative",
    "lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form"
  ],
  "statement": "Adopt a classical pure Yang–Mills model with spacetime $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$,\ncoordinates $x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3$ of length, orientation\n$dx^0\\wedge dx^1\\wedge dx^2\\wedge dx^3$, time orientation of increasing\n$x^0$, and Lorentz metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$. Use\n$c=\\hbar=1$, so $x^0=t$, the coordinate and spacetime lengths have unit\n$\\mathrm m$, and the natural action $S/\\hbar$ is dimensionless.\n\nFix the global structure group $G=SU(2)$, not its quotient $SO(3)$, a\nspecified smooth right principal $SU(2)$-bundle $\\pi:P\\to M$, and the single\nadmitted bundle sector $\\Sigma=\\{[P]\\}$. The matter-representation label set\nis empty, so there are no matter fields or current source. The Lie algebra is\n$\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ with basis $T_a=-i\\sigma_a/2$ and positive\n$\\operatorname{Ad}$-invariant form\n$\\kappa(X,Y)=-2\\operatorname{Tr}_2(XY)$, normalized by\n$\\kappa(T_a,T_b)=\\delta_{ab}$. The positive coupling $g_{\\mathrm{YM}}$ is a\nfixed dimensionless model parameter.\n\nA gauge field is a smooth principal connection $\\omega$ on $P$. In a local\nsection $s_i:U_i\\to P$, let $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and let\n$F_i=dA_i+\\frac12[A_i\\wedge A_i]$ be its curvature. Here the bracket is the\nalternating-form extension of the Lie bracket, and the local forms on\noverlaps satisfy the right-action transition convention\n$A_j=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}A_i+g_{ij}^{-1}dg_{ij}$ and\n$F_j=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}F_i$ when $s_j=s_i g_{ij}$. Thus\n$F_i$ represents one global $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$-valued two-form in the\nassociated adjoint bundle; the invariant form $\\kappa$ makes\n$\\kappa(F_i\\wedge *_\\eta F_i)$ a global scalar four-form.\n\nAdopt the local Lorentzian action density\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L_{\\mathrm{YM}}(A_i)\\,d^4x\n=-\\frac{1}{2g_{\\mathrm{YM}}^2}\\,\n\\kappa(F_i\\wedge *_\\eta F_i),\n\\qquad [A_i]=\\mathrm m^{-1},\\quad [F_i]=\\mathrm m^{-2}.\n$$\n\nFor any relatively compact region on which the density is integrable, the\naction is its integral. On all of $M$, the action is defined when that\nintegral converges. Local stationarity is tested through relative action\ndifferences under smooth compactly supported adjoint-bundle-valued\none-form variations; these differences have compact support and are finite.\nNo boundary values are imposed at infinity. On a finite region, admissible\nvariations vanish near its boundary. This is an adopted classical model and\nnormalization, not a theorem, measured law, or claim that a quantum\ncontinuum theory exists.",
  "definition": null
}
{
  "id": "pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-classical-gauge-invariance",
  "kind": "physics-theorem",
  "dependency_level": 3,
  "deps": [
    "post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model",
    "lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form",
    "def-gauge-group-of-a-smooth-principal-bundle",
    "prop-gauge-transformations-act-on-principal-connections",
    "def-qftx-principal-connection-form",
    "lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi",
    "def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative"
  ],
  "statement": "Let $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ have orientation\n$dx^0\\wedge dx^1\\wedge dx^2\\wedge dx^3$ and metric\n$\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$. Fix the pure $SU(2)$ model with a\nsmooth right principal bundle $P\\to M$, no matter fields, the form\n$\\kappa(X,Y)=-2\\operatorname{Tr}_2(XY)$ on $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$, and fixed\n$g_{\\mathrm{YM}}>0$. For a smooth connection with local curvature $F_i$,\nthe adopted action density is\n$-\\kappa(F_i\\wedge *_\\eta F_i)/(2g_{\\mathrm{YM}}^2)$.\n\nFor every smooth gauge transformation $\\Phi:P\\to P$ satisfying\n$\\pi\\circ\\Phi=\\pi$ and $\\Phi(pg)=\\Phi(p)g$, let $\\Phi_*H=d\\Phi(H)$ be its\naction on a principal connection $H$. Then the local curvature density is\nunchanged in every section, so every defined local action and every\nconvergent global action are invariant under $H\\mapsto\\Phi_*H$. More\nprecisely, for any local section $s_i:U_i\\to P$, define the smooth local map\n$v_i:U_i\\to SU(2)$ by\n$\\Phi^{-1}\\circ s_i=s_i v_i$. The transformed curvature components satisfy\n$F_i^{\\Phi}=\\operatorname{Ad}_{v_i^{-1}}F_i$. Each $v_i$ is local data; the\nstatement assumes no global map $M\\to SU(2)$ for a possibly nontrivial\nbundle.",
  "definition": null
}
{
  "id": "pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange",
  "kind": "physics-theorem",
  "dependency_level": 3,
  "deps": [
