items/lem-qftx-smooth-scalar-cauchy-evolution.md:123:The inequality follows from Cauchy–Schwarz for $H$ and $2ab\le a^2+b^2$; its condition is exactly the future causal covector condition for $g=-\alpha^2dt^2+h$. In a sufficiently small convex normal chart, the boundary of the backward causal cone of a vertex has this outward null conormal, by [F3]. Truncate below the vertex and above a spacelike base, apply the coordinate divergence theorem, and discard the nonnegative lateral flux. Zero source and zero Cauchy data on the base give zero energy by Gronwall, hence zero solution up to the vertex by continuity. Every truncated cone away from its vertex is piecewise smooth: its null side is the smooth exponential null cone and its intersections with the temporal levels are transverse. No regularity of a global cut locus is asserted or used. This proves local dependence on the actual metric causal cone, rather than only a larger coordinate cone. Bounded lower-order terms, including arbitrary $V$ and its derivatives on each compact set, change $C_0$ and require no sign assumption. [step 1.2, F3, F5, algebra]
