irst vertex. A flat $G$-valued edge cochain is a family $a_{ij}\\in G$ for each edge $i<j$ such that $a_{ij}a_{jk}=a_{ik}$ on every triangle. It defines the local coefficient system with fiber $A$ at each vertex and transport $\\rho_{a_{ij}}$ from vertex $j$ to vertex $i$.\n\nFor each integer $q\\geq0$ and local-coefficient $q$-cochain $c$, define the twisted coboundary on each ordered $(q+1)$-simplex by\n\n$$\n(\\delta_a c)_{i_0\\ldots i_{q+1}}=\\rho_{a_{i_0i_1}}c_{i_1\\ldots i_{q+1}}+\\sum_{r=1}^{q+1}(-1)^r c_{i_0\\ldots\\widehat{i_r}\\ldots i derivs 7
