+## Definition
+
+Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice, written $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$. Use natural units $\hbar=c=1$ on Minkowski spacetime $\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with metric $\eta=\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, orientation $dt\wedge dx^1\wedge dx^2\wedge dx^3$, and spatial orientation $\epsilon_{123}=1$. Fix the global gauge group $SU(2)$, not $SO(3)$, and the trivial right principal $SU(2)$-bundle over each spatial slice. Let
+
+$$T_a=-\frac{i}{2}\sigma_a\quad(a=1,2,3),\qquad \kappa(X,Y)=-2\operatorname{Tr}_2(XY),$$
+
+where $\sigma_a$ are the Pauli matrices and $\mathfrak{su}(2)$ has basis $T_1,T_2,T_3$. Thus $[T_a,T_b]=\epsilon_{abc}T_c$ and $\kappa(T_a,T_b)=\delta_{ab}$. The positive coupling $g$ is dimensionless. The scalar field is one real adjoint Higgs field: a smooth $\mathfrak{su}(2)$-valued map $\Phi$ on $\mathbb R^3$, viewed as the real form in the complexified adjoint representation. A gauge connection is a smooth $\mathfrak{su}(2)$-valued one-form $A=A_i dx^i$. In a local section change $s_j=s_i h_{ij}$, use the right-action convention $A_j=\operatorname{Ad}_{h_{ij}^{-1}}A_i+h_{ij}^{-1}dh_{ij}$ and $\Phi_j=\operatorname{Ad}_{h_{ij}^{-1}}\Phi_i$. Define
+
+$$F_{ij}=\partial_iA_j-\partial_jA_i+[A_i,A_j],\qquad D_i\Phi=\partial_i\Phi+[A_i,\Phi],\qquad B_i=\frac12\epsilon_{ijk}F_{jk}.$$
+
+The static Prasad–Sommerfield sector has $\partial_tA_i=\partial_t\Phi=0$, $A_0=0$, no other dynamical fields, and identically zero Higgs potential. Its adopted energy functional is
+
+$$E[A,\Phi]=\frac{1}{2g^2}\int_{\mathbb R^3}\sum_{i=1}^3\bigl(\kappa(B_i,B_i)+\kappa(D_i\Phi,D_i\Phi)\bigr)\,d^3x.$$
+
+The field dimensions are $[A_i]=[\Phi]=\mathrm{length}^{-1}$ and $[F_{ij}]=[B_i]=[D_i\Phi]=\mathrm{length}^{-2}$, so $E$ has dimension $\mathrm{length}^{-1}$. A configuration is finite-energy when this integral is finite.
+
+The boundary data fix a number $v>0$ of dimension $\mathrm{length}^{-1}$ and require $|\Phi|_\kappa\to v$ and $n_\infty(\omega):=\lim_{R\to\infty}\Phi(R\omega)/v$ to exist smoothly on the unit sphere $S^2$ of spatial directions. Here $|X|_\kappa^2:=\kappa(X,X)$. The limiting tangential covariant derivative of $n_\infty$ vanishes, and the limiting magnetic field lies in the pointwise stabilizer Lie algebra $\{X\in\mathfrak{su}(2):[X,n_\infty(\omega)]=0\}$. The stabilizer subgroup of $T_3$ is $U(1)=\{\exp(\theta T_3):\theta\in\mathbb R/(4\pi\mathbb Z)\}$. On closed northern and southern hemispheres choose smooth local lifts $u_N,u_S$ with $\operatorname{Ad}_{u_\alpha}T_3=n_\infty$; their equatorial transition is $u_S=u_N h$ with $h=\exp(\theta T_3)$. The limiting local connection and curvature forms are $C^1$ up to the equator, and the surface limit below exists. The admissible external Wilson probes include the fundamental doublet, on which $T_3$ has weights $\pm\tfrac12$; this specifies the electric probe lattice without adding a propagating fundamental matter field. Define the classical magnetic surface charge and its energy normalization by
+
+$$m:=\lim_{R\to\infty}\int_{S_R^2}\kappa(\Phi,B_i)\,\hat x_i\,dS,\qquad T:=g^{-2}m,$$
+
+where $\hat x=x/|x|$ is the outward unit normal and $dS$ is Euclidean area. The transition increment $\theta(2\pi)-\theta(0)$ is not assumed to be quantized in this definition. These are adopted classical model data; they assert no empirical law, quantum continuum construction, supersymmetry representation, or quantum BPS state.
+
+## Definition references
+
+[David Tong, §2.1, model and monopole conventions](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0509216)
+
+[Jeffrey A. Harvey, §§1.4 and 2.1–2.2, SU(2) Higgs model and monopole conventions](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9603086)
+
+[[def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data|Non-Abelian gauge group, bundle, and representation data]]
+
+[[def-qftx-principal-connection-form|Principal connection and right-action convention]]
+
+[[def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket|Lie-algebra-valued form bracket convention]]
+
+[[def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative|Associated covariant derivative]]
+
+[[prop-adjoint-is-a-smooth-lie-group-representation|Smooth adjoint representation]]
+
+[[lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form|Normalized invariant form on SU(2) (planned supplier)]]
+
+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$, the fixed global group $SU(2)$ and right principal bundle, smooth static fields $A,\Phi$, the stated Prasad–Sommerfield energy convention, the smooth limiting $U(1)$ reduction, and the surface-flux boundary condition.
+
+[A1] $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ is the Axiom of Countable Choice, used by the supplied gauge-geometry constructions. [[def-countable-choice]]
+
+[F1] The non-Abelian datum distinguishes the actual compact group and its global form from its Lie algebra alone, and records a specified right principal bundle and representation set. The present model selects $SU(2)$ and the real adjoint Higgs field. [[def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data]]
+
+[F2] A principal connection is a smooth right-invariant horizontal complement; its local connection forms obey $A_j=\operatorname{Ad}_{h_{ij}^{-1}}A_i+h_{ij}^{-1}dh_{ij}$. [[def-qftx-principal-connection-form]]
+
+[F3] For Lie-algebra-valued one-forms, $\tfrac12[A\wedge A](X,Y)=[A(X),A(Y)]$, which yields the displayed component curvature formula. [[def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket]]
+
+[F4] The adjoint action is a smooth group representation, and its associated covariant derivative has local form $d\Phi+[A,\Phi]$ on the real adjoint subspace. [[prop-adjoint-is-a-smooth-lie-group-representation]], [[def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative]]
+
+[A2] The planned supplier states that $\kappa(X,Y)=-2\operatorname{Tr}_2(XY)$ on this basis is a positive-definite, symmetric, $\operatorname{Ad}$-invariant real bilinear form with $\kappa(T_a,T_b)=\delta_{ab}$. Its batch-19 carrier and current readiness record are absent, so this model uses that exact interface conditionally and does not certify it as proved. [[lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form]]

