+The static Prasad–Sommerfield sector has $\partial_tA_i=\partial_t\Phi=0$, $A_0=0$, no other dynamical fields, and identically zero Higgs potential. Its adopted energy functional is
+
+$$E[A,\Phi]=\frac{1}{2g^2}\int_{\mathbb R^3}\sum_{i=1}^3\bigl(\kappa(B_i,B_i)+\kappa(D_i\Phi,D_i\Phi)\bigr)\,d^3x.$$
+
+The field dimensions are $[A_i]=[\Phi]=\mathrm{length}^{-1}$ and $[F_{ij}]=[B_i]=[D_i\Phi]=\mathrm{length}^{-2}$, so $E$ has dimension $\mathrm{length}^{-1}$. A configuration is finite-energy when this integral is finite.
+
+The boundary data fix a number $v>0$ of dimension $\mathrm{length}^{-1}$ and require $|\Phi|_\kappa\to v$ and $n_\infty(\omega):=\lim_{R\to\infty}\Phi(R\omega)/v$ to exist smoothly on the unit sphere $S^2$ of spatial directions. Here $|X|_\kappa^2:=\kappa(X,X)$. The limiting tangential covariant derivative of $n_\infty$ vanishes, and the limiting magnetic field lies in the pointwise stabilizer Lie algebra $\{X\in\mathfrak{su}(2):[X,n_\infty(\omega)]=0\}$. The stabilizer subgroup of $T_3$ is $U(1)=\{\exp(\theta T_3):\theta\in\mathbb R/(4\pi\mathbb Z)\}$. On closed northern and southern hemispheres choose smooth local lifts $u_N,u_S$ with $\operatorname{Ad}_{u_\alpha}T_3=n_\infty$; their equatorial transition is $u_S=u_N h$ with $h(\varphi)=\exp(\theta(\varphi)T_3)$, where $\varphi\in[0,2\pi]$ parametrizes the equator and $\theta:[0,2\pi]\to\mathbb R$ is a smooth lift. The limiting local connection and curvature forms are $C^1$ up to the equator, and the surface limit below exists. The admissible external Wilson probes include the fundamental doublet, on which $T_3$ has weights $\pm\tfrac12$; this specifies the electric probe lattice without adding a propagating fundamental matter field. Define the classical magnetic surface charge and its energy normalization by
+
+$$m:=\lim_{R\to\infty}\int_{S_R^2}\kappa(\Phi,B_i)\,\hat x_i\,dS,\qquad T:=g^{-2}m,$$
+
+where $\hat x=x/|x|$ is the outward unit normal and $dS$ is Euclidean area. The transition increment $\theta(2\pi)-\theta(0)$ is not assumed to be quantized in this definition. These are adopted classical model data; they assert no empirical law, quantum continuum construction, supersymmetry representation, or quantum BPS state.
+
+## Definition references
+
+[David Tong, §2.1, model and monopole conventions](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0509216)
+
+[Jeffrey A. Harvey, §§1.4 and 2.1–2.2, SU(2) Higgs model and monopole conventions](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9603086)
+
