+
+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$, the fixed global group $SU(2)$ and right principal bundle, smooth static fields $A,\Phi$, the stated Prasad–Sommerfield energy convention, the smooth limiting $U(1)$ reduction, and the surface-flux boundary condition.
+
+[A1] $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ is the Axiom of Countable Choice, used by the supplied gauge-geometry constructions. [[def-countable-choice]]
+
+[F1] The non-Abelian datum distinguishes the actual compact group and its global form from its Lie algebra alone, and records a specified right principal bundle and representation set. The present model selects $SU(2)$ and the real adjoint Higgs field. [[def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data]]
+
+[F2] A principal connection is a smooth right-invariant horizontal complement; its local connection forms obey $A_j=\operatorname{Ad}_{h_{ij}^{-1}}A_i+h_{ij}^{-1}dh_{ij}$. [[def-qftx-principal-connection-form]]
