research/plan-spec.json-15158-          "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$, let $(U,U_\\rho,\\tilde A,\\tilde B,M,K,\\delta,\\Psi_h)$ be analytic splitting data, and use the notation of [[def-cm-modified-log-coefficients-and-truncations]] and [[lem-cm-difference-operator-and-domain-loss-bound]]: $b=\\rho/(8N)$, $r_N=\\rho/(C_0MN)$ with $C_0=\\max\\{16,128d^2\\}$, the domains $D_k$, the difference operator $\\Delta_h$, the truncated logarithm $L_N(h)$ and the coefficient fields $X_j$, $1\\le j\\le N$. Then for every integer $N\\ge2$, every $|h|\\le r_N$ and every coordinate index $i$:\n\n1. $\\lVert\\Delta_h^kz_i\\rVert_{D_k}\\le2M|h|\\,q^{k-1}$ for $1\\le k\\le N$, where $q=C_dM|h|/b\\le1/4$.\n2. The function $h\\mapsto\\frac{(L_N(h)z_i)(Z)}{h}$, initially defined for $0<|h|\\le r_N$, extends holomorphically to the disc $|h|\\le r_N$, and\n $$\\left\\lvert\\frac{(L_N(h)z_i)(Z)}{h}\\right\\rvert\\le\\frac{2M}{1-q}\\le\\frac{8M}{3}\\qquad(|h|\\le r_N,\\ Z\\in D_N).$$\n3. For $1\\le j\\le N$ and every $Z\\in D_N$,\n $$\\max_i\\lvert(X_j)_i(Z)\\rvert\\le\\frac{8M}{3}\\,r_N^{-(j-1)},$$\n and the sharper estimate\n $$\\max_i\\lvert(X_j)_i(Z)\\rvert\\le\\frac{8M}{3}\\left(\\frac{C_0Mj}{\\rho}\\right)^{j-1},$$\n obtained for $j\\ge2$ by computing the $j$-th field with truncation order $j$, and for $j=1$ from $X_1=X_{\\tilde A}+X_{\\tilde B}$; the two bounds agree in the form $r_N^{-(j-1)}=(C_0MN/\\rho)^{j-1}$.\nThe corresponding Euclidean field bounds are these component bounds multiplied by $\\sqrt{2d}$.\n\n4. The field $X_j$ is independent of the truncation order: if $N,N'\\ge j$ then the $j$-th coefficient fields of $L_N$ and $L_{N'}$ agree on $D(\\rho/4)$.",
