research/plan-spec.json-16765-          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R^3)$ be the Borel sigma-algebra of $\\mathbb R^3$\n([[def-borel-sigma-algebra]]), let $\\nu$ be a measure on the measurable space\n$(\\mathbb R^3,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R^3))$ ([[def-measure]], [[def-measure-space]]) that is\n**finite** and **bounded**: $\\nu(\\mathbb R^3)<+\\infty$ and\n$\\nu\\bigl(\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\overline B_R(0)\\bigr)=0$ for some real $R>0$\n([[def-metric-ball]]). Put $m:=\\nu(\\mathbb R^3)\\in[0,+\\infty)$; nonnegativity follows from the\ndefinition of measure [[def-measure]]. If $m>0$, then $\\nu$ is a mass distribution in the sense of\n[[def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix]]. If $m=0$, then for every Borel set\n$E\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ one has $0\\le\\nu(E)\\le\\nu(\\mathbb R^3)=0$, so $\\nu$ is the zero measure.\nIntegrals against $\\nu$ are Lebesgue integrals as in [[def-integral-over-a-measurable-set]] and\n[[def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals]], defined componentwise for\nvector- and matrix-valued integrands. When $m>0$, recall that the inertia matrix of $\\nu$ is\n\n$$I(\\nu)=\\int\\bigl(\\lVert\\rho\\rVert_2^2I_3-\\rho\\rho^{\\mathsf T}\\bigr)\\,d\\nu(\\rho)\\in M_3(\\mathbb R),$$\n\nwith $I_3$ the identity matrix and entrywise integrals\n$I(\\nu)_{jk}=\\int(\\lVert\\rho\\rVert_2^2\\delta_{jk}-\\rho_j\\rho_k)\\,d\\nu$, where $\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_2$\nand the matrix conventions are those of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]],\n[[def-matrix-space]] and [[def-matrix-product-and-identity-matrix]].\n\n**Shifted integrand and inertia tensor about a point.** For $a\\in\\mathbb R^3$ define the\ncomponent functions\n\n$$G_a(\\rho)_{jk}:=\\lVert\\rho-a\\rVert_2^2\\,\\delta_{jk}-(\\rho_j-a_j)(\\rho_k-a_k)\\qquad(j,k\\in\\{1,2,3\\}),$$\n\nequivalently the matrix-valued function\n$G_a(\\rho)=\\lVert\\rho-a\\rVert_2^2I_3-(\\rho-a)(\\rho-a)^{\\mathsf T}$, and define the **inertia\ntensor of $\\nu$ about $a$** $I_\\nu(a)\\in M_3(\\mathbb R)$ by its entries\n\n$$I_\\nu(a)_{jk}:=\\int G_a(\\rho)_{jk}\\,d\\nu(\\rho).$$\n\nUnder the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]) each entry is\na finite real number; this is the content of [[lem-cm-inertia-tensor-about-a-point-is-finite]],\nwhich depends on this definition only for its notation. For $a=0$ the shifted integrand is the\nparent integrand $\\lVert\\rho\\rVert_2^2I_3-\\rho\\rho^{\\mathsf T}$. Thus\n$I_\\nu(0)=I(\\nu)$ when $m>0$; if $m=0$, the parent definition does not define $I(\\nu)$, while\nthe shifted integral remains defined and equals the zero matrix $0_{3\\times3}$ for every $a$.\n\n**Scope.** The definition names a mathematical function $a\\mapsto I_\\nu(a)$ from $\\mathbb R^3$ to\n$M_3(\\mathbb R)$ determined by any finite bounded Borel measure $\\nu$ and its coordinate origin.\nFor the zero measure this function is identically $0_{3\\times3}$. No physical body, unit system or\nmeasured mass is asserted. No translation identity for nonzero $a$ is asserted here; the centred,\npositive-total-mass case is proved separately on this page.",
research/plan-spec.json-16766-          "strategy": "Define the shifted integrand and its componentwise integral against the measure with the conventions of def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix; declare the finiteness result that makes the entries well-defined.",
--
