research/plan-spec.json-18680-          "statement": "Take $a=100$, so $L=\\sqrt{74}$, $k=1/2$, and let $r_+=1+\\sqrt{101}$ be the constant-code value of the all-$+1$ code. The fixed slope of the forward transform $\\Phi_y(h)=1/(2y-h)$ at $y=r_+$ is the small root of $h=1/(2r_+-h)$, i.e. of\n\n$$h^2-2r_+h+1=0:\\qquad h=r_+-\\sqrt{r_+^2-1}=\\frac1{r_++\\sqrt{r_+^2-1}},$$\n\nand one has $0<h<1/2$. Moreover $\\lambda=2L-k=2\\sqrt{74}-\\tfrac12>1$ and $\\Phi_{r_+}$ maps $[-1/2,1/2]$ into $[-\\lambda^{-1},\\lambda^{-1}]\\subseteq[-1/2,1/2]$ with Lipschitz constant $\\lambda^{-2}<1/2$.",
research/plan-spec.json-18681-          "strategy": "Exact algebra with sqrt(101) and sqrt(74) plus rational comparisons, checked against the defining inequalities of the slope lemma.",
--
research/plan-spec.json-18726-          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (finite-word codes and their homoclinic limits)",
research/plan-spec.json-18727-          "design_state": "completed-local-example",
research/plan-spec.json:18728:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-18729-          "statement": "Take $a=100$ and let $s\\in X_\\pm$ be the code with\n\n$$s_0=-1,\\qquad s_n=+1\\ (n\\ne0),$$\n\nthe single-flip code. Then $s$ is constant outside a finite set (indeed outside $\\{0\\}$), is not the constant code $\\bar{+1}$, and is not periodic: $S_\\pm^m s\\ne s$ for every $m\\ge1$, because the unique coordinate at which $S_\\pm^ms$ equals $-1$ is $-m\\ne0$ whereas $s$ equals $-1$ only at $0$. Consequently the coded point $z:=h(s)$ satisfies $z\\ne(r_+,r_+)$ and $F^m(z)\\ne z$ for every $m\\ge1$, while\n\n$$F^n(z)\\longrightarrow(r_+,r_+)\\quad(n\\to+\\infty\\ \\text{and}\\ n\\to-\\infty).$$",
research/plan-spec.json-18730-          "strategy": "Locality of the coding, the conjugacy's injectivity, and the convergence of constant tails to the fixed point.",
--
research/plan-spec.json-18779-          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#5 (the explicit delta=0 endpoint computation)",
