research/plan-spec.json-19227-          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, $h>0$, let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$, and let $v:O_h(\\Omega)\\to\\mathbb C^n$ be holomorphic with $|v|_{O_h(\\Omega)}\\le B$ where\n$$0\\le B\\le\\frac{h}{16n}.$$\nThen:\n\n1. **Existence and uniqueness.** For every $\\nu_+\\in O_{h/4}(\\Omega)$ there is exactly one $\\nu\\in O_{h/2}(\\Omega)$ with\n$$\\nu+v(\\nu)=\\nu_+.$$\n   The assignment $\\phi(\\nu_+):=\\nu$ defines a map $\\phi:O_{h/4}(\\Omega)\\to O_{h/2}(\\Omega)$ with $|\\phi(\\nu_+)-\\nu_+|_\\infty\\le B$ for every $\\nu_+$.\n2. **Holomorphy.** $\\phi$ is holomorphic on $O_{h/4}(\\Omega)$.\n3. **Derivative bounds.** With $D\\phi$ the complex Jacobian and the row-sum norm, for every $\\nu_+\\in O_{h/4}(\\Omega)$\n$$\\|D\\phi(\\nu_+)-I_n\\|\\le\\frac{16n}{7}\\,\\frac{B}{h},\\qquad\\text{equivalently}\\qquad h\\,\\|D\\phi(\\nu_+)-I_n\\|\\le\\frac{16n}{7}B.$$",
research/plan-spec.json-19228-          "strategy": "direct; solve the frequency equation by the contraction principle on a complex ball of radius $2B$, prove holomorphy from the uniformly convergent iteration, and differentiate the defining identity to bound the Jacobian.",
--
