research/plan-spec.json-19521-          "statement": "Let $n\\ge2$, $\\tau>n-1$, $\\mu:=\\tau+3n+2$, $\\alpha>0$, $s_0>0$,\n$0<\\sigma_0\\le\\min(1,s_0/24)$, and let $c_1\\in(0,1]$ be the one-step smallness\nconstant (the constant $c$ of the estimates of\n[[lem-kam-generator-flow-and-remainder-bound]]). Let the following\ndata be given.\n\n1. An open set $U\\subseteq\\mathbb C^n$, a compact set $K\\subseteq U\\cap\\mathbb R^n$, a radius $0<r_0\\le1$ with $\\{J\\in\\mathbb C^n:\\operatorname{dist}_\\infty(J,K)<2r_0\\}\\subseteq U$, a nonempty set $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ and a conjugation-invariant open complex neighbourhood $\\Omega'\\subseteq\\mathbb C^n$ containing $\\Omega$; and a holomorphic map $b:\\Omega'\\to U$ with $Dh(b(\\nu))=\\nu$ for every $\\nu\\in\\Omega'$, where $h:U\\to\\mathbb C$ is holomorphic and $b(\\Omega)+(B_{r_0}\\cap\\mathbb R^n)\\subseteq K$. (In the applications $b=(Dh)^{-1}$ on a regular frequency patch, supplied by the real analytic inverse function theorem; here it is part of the data.)\n2. A constant $M_2\\ge1$ with $|I^{\\mathsf T}D^2h(J)\\,I|\\le M_2|I|_\\infty^2$ for all $I\\in\\mathbb C^n$ and all $J\\in\\{J':\\operatorname{dist}_\\infty(J',K)<2r_0\\}$.\n3. A holomorphic function $F$ on $\\{J:\\operatorname{dist}_\\infty(J,K)<2r_0\\}\\times S_{s_0}$, $2\\pi$-periodic in $\\vartheta$, with $|F|\\le\\varepsilon$.\n\nPut $r:=\\sqrt{\\varepsilon/M_2}$ and assume $0<r\\le r_0$. Then:\n\n1. **Taylor decomposition.** For every $\\nu\\in\\Omega$ and $|I|_\\infty\\le r$,\n$$h(b(\\nu)+I)=h(b(\\nu))+\\nu\\cdot I+P_h(I,\\nu),\\qquad |P_h(I,\\nu)|\\le M_2|I|_\\infty^2 .$$\n2. **Effective perturbation.** The function\n$$G(I,\\vartheta,\\nu):=h(b(\\nu)+I)-h(b(\\nu))-\\nu\\cdot I+F(b(\\nu)+I,\\vartheta)$$\nis holomorphic on $D_{r,s_0,h_0'}(\\Omega)$ whenever $O_{h_0'}(\\Omega)\\subseteq\\Omega'$ and $b(O_{h_0'}(\\Omega))+B_r\\subseteq\\{J:\\operatorname{dist}_\\infty(J,K)<2r_0\\}$, $2\\pi$-periodic in $\\vartheta$, and satisfies\n$$|G|\\le M_2r^2+\\varepsilon=2\\varepsilon .$$\n3. **$\\alpha^2$-smallness.** If\n$$\\varepsilon\\le\\frac{c_1^2}{4}\\cdot\\frac{\\alpha^2\\sigma_0^{2\\mu}}{M_2},$$\nthen $|G|\\le c_1\\alpha r\\sigma_0^{\\mu}$; equivalently the relative smallness $E:=|G|/(\\alpha r\\sigma_0^{\\mu})$ satisfies $E\\le c_1$.\n4. **Transfer to the physical Hamiltonian.** Let $H(p,\\vartheta):=h(p)+F(p,\\vartheta)$ and suppose that the parameter Hamiltonian\n$$H_{\\mathrm{par}}(I,\\vartheta,\\nu):=h(b(\\nu))+\\nu\\cdot I+G(I,\\vartheta,\\nu)$$\nsatisfies the hypotheses of [[thm-parameter-kam-torus-invariance-and-lagrangianity]] on $D_{r,s_0,h_0'}(\\Omega_{\\alpha,\\tau})$ (same sequences, same one-step construction, with $P_0:=G$), with limit phase family $\\Phi_\\infty=(\\Phi_I,\\Phi_\\vartheta)$ and limit original-parameter map $\\chi_\\infty$. Then for every $\\nu\\in\\Omega_{\\alpha,\\tau}$ the physical family\n$$\\Psi_\\nu(\\vartheta):=\\bigl(b(\\chi_\\infty(\\nu))+\\Phi_I(0,\\vartheta,\\nu),\\ \\Phi_\\vartheta(0,\\vartheta,\\nu)\\bigr)$$\nsatisfies\n$$X_H\\bigl(\\Psi_\\nu(\\vartheta)\\bigr)=\\sum_{j=1}^n\\nu_j\\,\\partial_{\\vartheta_j}\\Psi_\\nu(\\vartheta),\\qquad \\Psi_\\nu^*\\omega=0,$$\nwhere $\\omega=\\sum_jd\\vartheta_j\\wedge dI_j$ and $X_H=(-H_\\vartheta,H_I)$ is taken in the action-angle coordinates $(p,\\vartheta)$; that is, the image is an invariant Lagrangian torus of the physical Hamiltonian $H$ with frequency $\\nu$.",
research/plan-spec.json-19522-          "strategy": "direct; expand the integrable part to second order along the action segment, bound by the Hessian constant, choose $r$ to balance the two error terms, and translate the parameter family back to the physical variables.",
