research/plan-spec.json-225092-          "statement": "Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be the nonempty bounded connected smooth Euclidean domain of the positive matrix boundary problem, with $d\\ge1$. For a smooth real-valued function $u$ on $\\overline\\Omega$, define the Euclidean Laplacian by $\\Delta u:=\\sum_{a=1}^d\\partial_a^2u$ and call $u$ **harmonic** on $\\Omega$ when $\\Delta u=0$ there. In matrix size $n=2$, define\n\n$$\\Phi_u(x):=\\begin{pmatrix}e^{u(x)}&0\\\\0&e^{-u(x)}\\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nThen $\\Phi_u$ is a smooth map into the positive Hermitian determinant-one matrices, and it satisfies $\\operatorname{div}(\\Phi_u^{-1}d\\Phi_u)=0$ exactly when $u$ is harmonic. Moreover, if $u,v\\in C^\\infty(\\overline\\Omega,\\mathbb R)$ are harmonic and $\\Phi_u=\\Phi_v$ at every point of $\\partial\\Omega$, then $\\Phi_u=\\Phi_v$ on $\\overline\\Omega$ (and hence $u=v$ there).",
