research/plan-spec.json-225467-          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice for the smooth tangent-bundle convention in the\nLorentzian suppliers below. Let $(M,g,N)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian\nfour-manifold of signature $(-,+,+,+)$, and let $\\iota:S\\hookrightarrow M$ be\na smooth embedded two-manifold without boundary whose induced form\n$q:=\\iota^*g$ is positive definite. Write\n$$\\mathcal N_pS:=\\{v\\in T_pM:g_p(v,X)=0\\text{ for every }X\\in T_pS\\}.$$\nThen $\\mathcal N S$ is a smooth rank-two Lorentzian vector bundle. Around each\n$p\\in S$ there are smooth future null normal fields $\\ell,k$ with\n$$g(\\ell,\\ell)=g(k,k)=0,\\qquad g(\\ell,k)=-2.$$\nOn an overlap where two such ordered pairs select the same future null ray,\nthey differ by a smooth boost $\\ell'=e^f\\ell$, $k'=e^{-f}k$; if their ray\nlabels are exchanged, the same rule holds after interchanging the labels.\nNo global null normal pair is asserted.\n\nHere a **smooth null hypersurface** $H\\subset M$ means a smooth embedded\nthree-dimensional submanifold without boundary such that, at every $p\\in H$,\nthe restriction $g_p|_{T_pH}$ is positive semidefinite of rank two. Its radical\nis the one-dimensional subspace\n$$\\operatorname{Rad}(g_p|_{T_pH}):=\\{v\\in T_pH:g_p(v,w)=0\\text{ for every }w\\in T_pH\\}.$$\nA **smooth future null normal field** on $H$ is a smooth nowhere-zero section\n$\\ell$ of this radical line, with $g_p(\\ell_p,N_p)<0$. Thus\n$$T_pH=\\ell_p^\\perp,\\qquad (T_pH)^\\perp=\\operatorname{Rad}(g_p|_{T_pH})=\\mathbb R\\ell_p;$$\nin particular, the normal space of a null hypersurface is a null line, not a\nLorentzian two-plane. A **spacelike section** $S$ of $H$ is a smooth embedded\ntwo-manifold $S\\subset H$ such that $q:=g|_{TS}$ is positive definite and\n$$T_pH=T_pS\\oplus\\mathbb R\\ell_p\\qquad(p\\in S).$$\nThe condition says that $S$ is transverse to the null generators.\nThe **null generator curves** are integral curves $\\gamma$ of $\\ell$, meaning\n$\\dot\\gamma=\\ell\\circ\\gamma$; when $D_\\ell\\ell=0$, their parameter is affine.\nFor fields defined only along $H$ or a surface $S$, covariant derivatives\n$\\nabla_X\\ell$ use the pullback of the metric-selected connection.\n\nFor a smooth future null normal field $\\ell$ on $H$, the quotient\n$$\\mathscr S_p:=\\ell_p^\\perp/\\mathbb R\\ell_p,\\qquad p\\in H,$$\nis a smooth rank-two bundle with positive metric\n$$\\bar q_p([X],[Y]):=g_p(X,Y).$$\nThe normal line is $\\mathbb R\\ell_p$; the auxiliary null direction used in the\nproof below is not a second normal to $H$. If $\\ell$ is **affinely geodesic**,\nmeaning $D_\\ell\\ell=0$ along its integral curves, the map\n$$B_p:\\mathscr S_p\\to\\mathscr S_p,\\qquad [X]\\mapsto[\\nabla_X\\ell]$$\nis well-defined and self-adjoint with respect to $\\bar q$, that is,\n$\\bar q(Bu,v)=\\bar q(u,Bv)$. On a spacelike section $S$ of $H$, the quotient\nmap $T_pS\\to\\mathscr S_p$, $X\\mapsto[X]$, is an isometry; it is an isomorphism\nby transversality, and $\\bar q([X],[Y])=q(X,Y)$. For a smooth future null\nnormal $\\ell$ to a spacelike surface $S$, define\n$$\\chi_\\ell(X,Y):=g(\\nabla_X\\ell,Y)\\qquad(X,Y\\in T_pS);$$\nwhere $\\nabla_X\\ell$ is computed with the pullback of the metric-selected\nconnection to $S$. This is a well-defined symmetric bilinear form. Along an\naffine generator, for a screen section $[X]$, the screen derivative\n$\\mathcal D_\\ell[X]:=[D_\\ell X]$ is independent of the representative and\npreserves the screen metric in the sense that\n$$\\ell\\bigl(\\bar q([X],[Y])\\bigr)=\\bar q(\\mathcal D_\\ell[X],[Y])+\\bar q([X],\\mathcal D_\\ell[Y]).$$\nFor a smooth function $f$ on the section, the rescaling\n$\\ell'=e^f\\ell$, $k'=e^{-f}k$ of a normalized null normal pair is a boost; it\nobeys\n$$\\chi_{e^f\\ell}=e^f\\chi_\\ell.$$\n\n",
