research/plan-spec.json-225555-          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice for the Lorentzian supplier conventions. Let $(M,g,N)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold, let $S$ be a smooth spacelike two-surface, and let $F:U\\times J\\to M$ be a smooth null geodesic hypersurface congruence from an open section $U\\subseteq S$, as defined in [[def-gr-fx-null-screen-geometry]]. Write $\\ell=\\partial_\\lambda F$ and fix $p\\in U$. Before the first focal instant let $A_\\lambda:T_pS\\to\\mathscr S_{F(p,\\lambda)}$ be the screen Jacobi map, $B=A'A^{-1}$ the optical endomorphism, $\\theta=\\operatorname{tr}B$ its expansion, and $\\sigma=B-\\frac12\\theta\\,\\mathrm{id}$ its shear. Let $\\operatorname{Ric}$ be the Ricci tensor in [[def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors]]. Then, along the generator $\\gamma(\\lambda)=F(p,\\lambda)$ and before the first focal instant,\n$$\\frac{d\\theta}{d\\lambda}=-\\frac{\\theta^2}{2}-|\\sigma|_{\\bar q}^2-\\operatorname{Ric}(\\ell,\\ell).$$\nIf $\\operatorname{Ric}(\\ell,\\ell)\\ge0$ along the generator and $\\theta(0)<0$, then a first focal instant occurs by affine parameter\n$$\\lambda_*=\\frac{2}{|\\theta(0)|},$$\nprovided the smooth congruence and generator are defined through $\\lambda_*$. Here a focal instant means that the screen Jacobi map loses rank; the conclusion is local along this generator and asserts no curvature singularity.",
