research/plan-spec.json-225934-          "physical_scope": "Conditional mathematical identity for smooth compact vacuum conformal data with zero cosmological constant; it proves constraint equivalence only and no existence or spacetime development theorem.",
research/plan-spec.json:225935:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-225936-          "statement": "Let $(h,K)$ be the vacuum conformal constraint data of the definition. Then\n$\\operatorname{tr}_hK=\\tau$ and the momentum residual vanishes:\n$$\\mathcal M_j(h,K)=0.$$\nThe Hamiltonian residual is\n$$\\mathcal H(h,K)=0\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad -8\\widetilde\\Delta\\phi+\\widetilde R\\,\\phi-|\\widetilde\\sigma|_{\\widetilde h}^2\\phi^{-7} +\\frac{2}{3}\\tau^2\\phi^5=0.$$\nThe displayed scalar equation is the **Lichnerowicz equation** for these\nconstant-mean-curvature (CMC) vacuum data. Here CMC means that the trace\n$\\operatorname{tr}_hK$ is spatially constant; its value is $\\tau$.",
research/plan-spec.json-225937-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-225980-          },
research/plan-spec.json-225981-          "physical_scope": "Exact algebraic solution of the zero-cosmological-constant CMC vacuum constraint equation in the stated constant-coefficient case; it is not a universal solvability theorem.",
research/plan-spec.json:225982:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-225983-          "statement": "Let the vacuum conformal data be as in the definition, so that\n$\\widetilde\\sigma$ is TT with respect to $\\widetilde h$. Suppose the\nconformal metric has $\\widetilde R=0$ and\n$|\\widetilde\\sigma|_{\\widetilde h}^2=A$ is a positive constant, with constant\n$\\tau\\ne0$. Then the Lichnerowicz equation has exactly one positive constant\nsolution,\n$$\\phi_0=\\left(\\frac{3A}{2\\tau^2}\\right)^{1/12}.$$\nWith a fixed length unit, $[A]=[\\tau^2]=\\mathrm m^{-2}$, so $\\phi_0$ is\ndimensionless. Uniqueness is only among positive constant solutions; no\nuniqueness claim is made for arbitrary positive functions.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-225984-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-226035-          },
research/plan-spec.json-226036-          "physical_scope": "Fourier analysis of the linearized vacuum CMC constraint operator at the stated flat-torus solution; it proves a positive linear inverse and no nonlinear nearby-data existence theorem.",
research/plan-spec.json:226037:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-226038-          "statement": "Let $\\Sigma=\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$ with dimensionless coordinates\n$x^i\\pmod{2\\pi}$ and flat conformal metric\n$\\widetilde h=L_*^2\\sum_{i=1}^3(dx^i)^2$, where $L_*>0$ is a fixed reference\nlength. Suppose $\\widetilde\\sigma$ has constant squared norm $A>0$ and\n$\\tau\\ne0$, and let $\\phi_0$ be the positive constant solution in the preceding\nproposition. Put\n$$c:=7A\\phi_0^{-8}+\\frac{10}{3}\\tau^2\\phi_0^4>0.$$\nThe directional linearization of the Lichnerowicz scalar expression at\n$\\phi_0$ is\n$$\\mathcal A v=-8\\widetilde\\Delta v+cv.$$\nIt is strictly positive on nonzero smooth real $v$. For every integer $s\\ge2$,\nthe same differential expression, interpreted using weak derivatives, defines\na bounded bijection\n$\\mathcal A:H^{s+2}(\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi})\\to H^s(\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi})$. With\nFourier coefficients relative to the normalized torus measure, its inverse is\n$$\\widehat{\\mathcal A^{-1}f}(k)= \\frac{\\widehat f(k)}{8L_*^{-2}|k|^2+c},\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z^3,$$\nand, for $N_s(f)^2:=\\sum_k(1+|k|^2)^s|\\widehat f(k)|^2$,\n$$N_{s+2}(\\mathcal A^{-1}f)\\le \\min\\{8L_*^{-2},c\\}^{-1}N_s(f).$$\nThe equivalent derivative Sobolev norms therefore give a bounded\n$H^s\\to H^{s+2}$ inverse. This linear result does not assert nonlinear\ndifferentiability of the constraint map or nearby-data solvability.",
research/plan-spec.json-226039-          "provenance": {
