research/plan-spec.json-226267-          "statement": "Let $M$ be a smooth four-manifold, let $g$ be a smooth symmetric covariant $2$-tensor on $M$, and let $\\Phi:M\\to M$ be a smooth diffeomorphism. The pullback tensor $\\Phi^*g$ is the smooth covariant $2$-tensor defined at each $p\\in M$ by\n\n$$(\\Phi^*g)_p(X,Y):=g_{\\Phi(p)}(d\\Phi_pX,d\\Phi_pY),\\qquad X,Y\\in T_pM.$$\n\nWhen $g$ is Lorentzian, this formula defines the metric components seen in the coordinate representative obtained by $\\Phi$. Equality of $\\Phi^*g$ and $g$ means equality of the bilinear forms on each tangent space, not equality of their component arrays in a chosen chart.",
research/plan-spec.json-226268-          "strategy": "Definition: objects and hypotheses specified; no proof obligation.",
