research/plan-spec.json-226387-          "statement": "Let $s\\ge5$ be an integer and let $J=[0,T]$, $T>0$, be a compact slab for one unforced smooth symmetric-hyperbolic reduction and the fixed gauge of `def-gr-fx-fixed-gauge-data-topology`. Let $z_n,z$ be classical solutions with the same coefficient family, gauge, matter branch and reconstruction rule. Assume their states lie in one compact admissible set, their $H^s$ and time-derivative norms have a common finite bound, and their initial data converge in $H^{s-1}$. Take $g_n,g$ to be the $g_{ab}$ components of those first-order states in the common coordinates. Then $g_n\\to g$ in $C^1(J\\times\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi})$.\n\nPut $M=J\\times\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$. Fix a compact parameter interval $I=[a,b]$ with $a<b$ and a common coordinate chart $(U,x)$ with closure in $(0,T)\\times\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$. Its position-velocity space is $TU=\\{(p,v):p\\in U,\\ v\\in T_pM\\}$, with the topology transported by $(p,v)\\mapsto(x(p),dx_pv)\\in x(U)\\times\\mathbb R^4$. Fix a compact subset $K\\subset TU$. If affinely parametrized future timelike $C^2$ geodesics $\\gamma_n:I\\to M$ of $g_n$ have initial position-velocity data converging to those of a $g$-geodesic $\\gamma$, and all the position-velocity lifts $\\lambda\\mapsto(\\gamma_n(\\lambda),\\dot\\gamma_n(\\lambda))$, including that of $\\gamma$, stay in $K$, then $\\gamma_n\\to\\gamma$ in $C^1(I)$ in chart components.\n\nFinally, assume the curves are future timelike for their respective metrics, share the fixed time orientation and constant $c>0$ of `def-gr-timelike-worldline-and-proper-time`, and have a uniform timelike margin\n$$g_n(\\dot\\gamma_n(\\lambda),\\dot\\gamma_n(\\lambda))\\le-\\eta<0\\qquad(n\\ge1,\\ \\lambda\\in I).$$\nThen their proper times converge:\n$$\\frac1c\\int_a^b\\sqrt{-g_n(\\dot\\gamma_n,\\dot\\gamma_n)}\\,d\\lambda\\longrightarrow\\frac1c\\int_a^b\\sqrt{-g(\\dot\\gamma,\\dot\\gamma)}\\,d\\lambda.$$\nAll conclusions concern a fixed finite slab and a fixed coordinate gauge; they assert no uniformity as $T\\to\\infty$ and no identification of arbitrary coordinate representatives.",
research/plan-spec.json-226388-          "strategy": "direct",
