research/plan-spec.json-226471-          "statement": "Let $M=\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$ have coordinates $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$, with $x^0$ measured in metres and the angular $x^i$ dimensionless, and time orientation $N=\\partial_0$. For the SI reading fix $c>0$ with units $\\mathrm m\\,\\mathrm s^{-1}$ and take the parameter $\\lambda$ and lengths $L,\\ell>0$ in metres; then proper-time increments have units of seconds. This fixes units only and asserts no measured value or clock law. The flat Lorentzian metric\n$$g=-(dx^0)^2+L^2\\bigl((dx^1)^2+(dx^2)^2+(dx^3)^2\\bigr)$$\nhas $g_{00}=-1$ dimensionless and spatial components with units of square metres. Let $0<|\\epsilon|<1$ and define the smooth spatial diffeomorphism\n$$\\Phi_\\epsilon(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)=(x^0,x^1+\\epsilon\\sin x^1,x^2,x^3),$$\nwhere the periodic lift of its second component descends to the circle. Its pullback metric has\n$$(\\Phi_\\epsilon^*g)_{11}=L^2(1+\\epsilon\\cos x^1)^2\\ne L^2$$\nat, for example, $x^1=0$, so the coordinate components change. Yet for the time-axis curve $\\gamma(\\lambda)=(\\lambda,x_*)$, $0\\le\\lambda\\le\\ell$, for a fixed $x_*\\in\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$, the proper time computed from $\\Phi_\\epsilon^*g$ along $\\gamma$ equals the proper time computed from $g$ along $\\Phi_\\epsilon\\circ\\gamma$; both are $\\ell/c$. This is an exact diffeomorphism comparison. The fixed-gauge Sobolev estimate concerns coordinate fields in one gauge and does not itself identify arbitrary coordinate representatives.\n\n```tikzcd\n\\begin{tikzcd}\n[0,\\ell] \\arrow[r,\"\\gamma\"] \\arrow[dr,\"\\Phi_\\epsilon\\circ\\gamma\"'] & (M,\\Phi_\\epsilon^*g) \\arrow[d,\"\\Phi_\\epsilon\"] \\\\\n& (M,g)\n\\end{tikzcd}\n```\nThe diagram commutes because its two paths send $\\lambda$ to $\\Phi_\\epsilon(\\gamma(\\lambda))$. The vertical arrow is an isometry by the pullback definition; this diagram records the comparison and is not used as a proof.",
research/plan-spec.json-226472-          "strategy": "direct",
