research/plan-spec.json-226760-          "statement": "Let $M>0$ be a mass in kilograms and put $m=G_NM/c^2$, a length. On the end $E=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:r=|x|>m/2\\}$, take the standard isotropic Schwarzschild slice data\n$$u=1+\\frac{m}{2r},\\qquad h=u^4\\delta,\\qquad K=0.$$\nHere “time-symmetric” means precisely $K=0$. With the fixed Cartesian end chart and unit asymptotic time normalization $x^0=ct$, the ADM energy is $Mc^2$ joules.",
research/plan-spec.json-226761-          "provenance": {
