research/plan-spec.json-226869-          "physical_scope": "Formal smooth asymptotically flat vacuum Bondi data at a null end; no global vacuum existence, exact finite-radius waveform, empirical claim, or conclusion about nature is asserted.",
research/plan-spec.json:226870:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-226871-          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice for the smooth Lorentzian tangent-bundle conventions of the suppliers. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval, $r_0>0$, and $\\mathcal E=I\\times(r_0,\\infty)\\times S^2$, where $S^2=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:|x|=1\\}$ has its unit round metric $q_{AB}$ and area form $d\\Omega$. Let $D_A$ be the Levi-Civita covariant derivative of $q$, and raise angular indices with $q^{AB}$. A **Bondi-Sachs end** is a smooth Lorentzian metric on $\\mathcal E$ written in coordinates $(u,r,x^A)$, $A,B=1,2$, as\n\n$$g=-\\left(e^{2\\beta}\\frac Vr-r^2\\gamma_{AB}U^AU^B\\right)du^2-2e^{2\\beta}du\\,dr-2r^2\\gamma_{AB}U^Bdu\\,dx^A+r^2\\gamma_{AB}dx^A dx^B,$$\n\nwhere $\\beta,V,U^A,\\gamma_{AB}$ are smooth, $\\gamma_{AB}$ is positive definite, $\\gamma^{AC}\\gamma_{CB}=\\delta^A_B$, and $\\det(\\gamma_{AB})=\\det(q_{AB})$. Thus $u=\\mathrm{constant}$ are outgoing null hypersurfaces, $r$ is the area radius, and $x^A$ are constant along their null generators. This Bondi gauge has $g_{rr}=g_{rA}=0$.\n\nA **smooth Bondi expansion** is such an end with the differentiated uniform expansions\n\n$$\\gamma_{AB}=q_{AB}+\\frac{C_{AB}(u,x)}r+\\frac{P_{AB}(u,x)}{r^2}+O(r^{-3}),\\qquad \\beta=O(r^{-2}),\\qquad U^A=\\frac{U^A_{(2)}(u,x)}{r^2}+\\frac{U^A_{(3)}(u,x)}{r^3}+O(r^{-4}),\\qquad V=r-2m(u,x)+\\frac{V_{(1)}(u,x)}r+O(r^{-2}).$$\n\nHere $C_{AB}$, $P_{AB}$ and the displayed coefficients are smooth sphere fields on $I$; the determinant gauge imposes $q^{AB}C_{AB}=0$ and $q^{AB}P_{AB}=\\tfrac12 C_{AB}C^{AB}$. For every compact $I'\\subset I$, angular chart compact set, and derivative multi-index $\\alpha$ of total order at most two, the partial derivatives of each $O(r^{-k})$ remainder obey $\\partial_u^{\\alpha_u}D^{\\alpha_x}\\partial_r^{\\alpha_r}O(r^{-k})=O(r^{-k-\\alpha_r})$ uniformly as $r\\to\\infty$. Define the **mass aspect** by $m(u,x):=-\\tfrac12\\lim_{r\\to\\infty}(V(u,r,x)-r)$, the **Bondi shear** by $C_{AB}=\\lim_{r\\to\\infty}r(\\gamma_{AB}-q_{AB})$, the **Bondi news** by $N_{AB}:=\\partial_u C_{AB}$, and the **geometric Bondi mass** by $m_B(u):=\\frac1{4\\pi}\\int_{S^2}m(u,x)\\,d\\Omega$. The future null boundary used here is the formal $r\\to\\infty$ boundary $\\mathcal I^+=I\\times S^2$ with coordinates $(u,x^A)$; no conformal completion is included in this definition.\n\nA **vacuum Bondi expansion** is a smooth Bondi expansion whose Ricci tensor vanishes identically on the supplied end: $\\operatorname{Ric}_g(p)=0$ for every $p\\in\\mathcal E$. Equivalently, $\\operatorname{Ric}_{ab}(u,r,x)=0$ for every pair $a,b\\in\\{u,r,1,2\\}$ at every point of every Bondi coordinate chart, with no cosmological term. The curvature convention is $R(X,Y)Z=\\nabla_X\\nabla_YZ-\\nabla_Y\\nabla_XZ-\\nabla_{[X,Y]}Z$, $R(\\partial_c,\\partial_d)\\partial_b=R^a{}_{bcd}\\partial_a$, and $\\operatorname{Ric}_{bd}=R^a{}_{bad}$. This is a condition on the supplied metric, not an assertion of existence for prescribed boundary coefficients. Imposing only finitely many asymptotic coefficient equations does not assert membership in this vacuum subclass; formal boundary-data examples must state separately which equations they impose.",
research/plan-spec.json-226872-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-226905-          },
research/plan-spec.json-226906-          "physical_scope": "Defines the fixed-frame supertranslation action on formal smooth Bondi data; the full asymptotic symmetry group and its charge algebra are outside scope, and no distinguished ten-parameter subgroup of Minkowski translations and proper orthochronous Lorentz transformations is selected.",
research/plan-spec.json:226907:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-226908-          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice for the smooth Lorentzian boundary conventions inherited from [[def-gr-fx-bondi-expansion]]. On its formal boundary $\\mathcal I^+=I\\times S^2$, let $\\ell_{\\mathcal I}=\\partial_u$ be the null-generator direction and let $q_{AB}$ be the unit round metric on the cuts; the degenerate boundary metric is $q_{AB}dx^A dx^B$ with kernel $\\mathbb R\\ell_{\\mathcal I}$. A **fixed Bondi frame** here means the chosen Bondi-Sachs chart and gauge $(u,r,x^A)$ of [[def-gr-fx-bondi-expansion]], including $g_{rr}=g_{rA}=0$ and $\\det\\gamma=\\det q$, with the round cut metric $q_{AB}$ held fixed. It is a chart/gauge choice, not an observer congruence or tetrad. An **infinitesimal supertranslation** is the asymptotic vector field parametrized by a smooth real function $f:S^2\\to\\mathbb R$ whose leading boundary action is $\\delta_fu=f(x)$ and whose leading bulk generator is\n\n$$\\xi_f=f\\,\\partial_u-\\frac1rD^Af\\,\\partial_A+\\frac12D^AD_Af\\,\\partial_r+O(r^{-1})\\partial_u+O(r^{-2})\\partial_A+O(r^{-1})\\partial_r.$$\n\nThe displayed leading terms preserve Bondi gauge and the fixed round cut metric to the asymptotic orders used here; the omitted terms are not part of this definition. We use the active convention $\\delta_f=\\mathcal L_{\\xi_f}$. Its action on the shear and news of [[def-gr-fx-bondi-expansion]] is\n\n$$\\delta_f C_{AB}=fN_{AB}-2D_AD_Bf+q_{AB}D^CD_Cf,\\qquad \\delta_f N_{AB}=f\\,\\partial_uN_{AB}.$$\n\nThe **finite active boundary supertranslation** with parameter $f$ is the map $\\Phi_f(u,x)=(u+f(x),x)$ on\n$$\\mathcal D_f:=\\{(u,x)\\in I\\times S^2:u+f(x)\\in I\\}.$$\nIt is a diffeomorphism from $\\mathcal D_f$ onto $\\mathcal D_{-f}$, with inverse $\\Phi_{-f}$. If $I=\\mathbb R$, it is a diffeomorphism of all of $\\mathcal I^+$; for a shorter retarded-time interval the action is defined on this overlap only. In the same active convention, its induced action on the boundary shear and news is\n\n$$C^{(f)}_{AB}(u,x)=C_{AB}(u+f(x),x)-2D_AD_Bf(x)+q_{AB}D^CD_Cf(x),\\qquad N^{(f)}_{AB}(u,x)=N_{AB}(u+f(x),x),\\quad (u,x)\\in\\mathcal D_f.$$\n\nDifferentiating these formulas for the parameter $tf$ at $t=0$ recovers the infinitesimal formulas above. This definition gives only the boundary action and induced shear/news; it does not specify the full finite bulk coordinate transformation.\n\nThe function $f$ carries length units when the retarded coordinate $u$ is read in SI geometric coordinates; the sphere derivatives and angular coordinates are dimensionless. The Hessian term is trace-free because $q^{AB}q_{AB}=2$. When $N_{AB}=0$, an infinitesimal supertranslation therefore changes a time-independent shear by the sphere trace-free Hessian while leaving the news zero.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-226909-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-226946-          },
research/plan-spec.json-226947-          "physical_scope": "Conditional coefficient identity for a smooth Ricci-flat Bondi expansion; no global vacuum solution, radiation measurement, or physical validity claim is asserted.",
research/plan-spec.json:226948:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-226949-          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice for the smooth Lorentzian bundle conventions of the suppliers. Let a vacuum Bondi expansion be as in [[def-gr-fx-bondi-expansion]], with $R_{ab}=0$ in the curvature convention of [[def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors]]. Then, for the mass aspect $m$, shear $C_{AB}$, news $N_{AB}=\\partial_uC_{AB}$, unit sphere metric $q_{AB}$ and its Levi-Civita derivative $D_A$ specified there,\n\n$$\\partial_um=\\frac14D_AD_BN^{AB}-\\frac18N_{AB}N^{AB}.$$\n\nThe identity is the leading supplementary vacuum Einstein coefficient at future null infinity; it is not an exact finite-radius equation.",
research/plan-spec.json-226950-          "provenance": {
