research/plan-spec.json-227762-          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the tangent-bundle smooth structure of the\nLorentzian conventions.\n\nLet $(\\mathcal M,g,N)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold with\nits metric-selected connection $\\nabla$. A smooth symmetric covariant\n$2$-tensor field $K_{ab}$ is a **rank-two Killing tensor** when\n\n$$\\nabla_{(a}K_{bc)}:=\\frac13\\left(\\nabla_aK_{bc}+\\nabla_bK_{ca}+\\nabla_cK_{ab}\\right)=0.$$\n\nFor a smooth curve $\\gamma:I\\to\\mathcal M$ with open interval domain and affine\nparameter $\\lambda$, write $v=\\dot\\gamma$. If $\\nabla_vv=0$, the curve is an\naffinely parametrized geodesic, and $K_{ab}v^av^b$ is its associated quadratic\ngeodesic integral. It is called **reducible** if it is a finite constant\nlinear combination of $g_{ab}$ and symmetric products\n$\\xi^\\flat\\odot\\eta^\\flat$, where $\\xi,\\eta$ are Killing fields,\n$\\xi^\\flat:=g(\\xi,\\cdot)$, and\n$\\alpha\\odot\\beta:=(\\alpha\\otimes\\beta+\\beta\\otimes\\alpha)/2$.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-227763-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-227804-          },
research/plan-spec.json-227805-          "physical_scope": "Pure mathematical contraction convention; it asserts no conservation, positivity, matter realization, or empirical result.",
research/plan-spec.json:227806:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-227807-          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the tangent-bundle smooth structure of the\nLorentzian conventions.\n\nLet $(\\mathcal M,g,N)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold, let\n$U\\subseteq\\mathcal M$ be open, let $S_{ab}$ be a smooth symmetric covariant\n$2$-tensor field on $U$, and let $X$ be a smooth Killing field on $U$. For\n$X_b:=g_{bc}X^c$ and $S^{ab}:=g^{ac}g^{bd}S_{cd}$, define the\n**Killing-multiplier current** by\n\n$$j_X^a:=-S^{ab}X_b.$$\n\nAt a point $p\\in U$ and for an observer $n\\in T_p\\mathcal M$ with\n$g_p(n,n)=-1$ and $n$ future-directed, define the associated\n**Killing-multiplier density** by\n\n$$\\rho_X(p;n):=-g_p(n,j_X)=S_{ab}(p)n^aX^b.$$\n\nThe current and density are defined for every such $S,X,n$. The definition\nimposes no conservation equation, sign condition, or coercivity property.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-227808-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-227853-          },
research/plan-spec.json-227854-          "physical_scope": "Pure geometric verification of the metric datum; no Einstein equation, black-hole uniqueness statement, or observation is asserted.",
research/plan-spec.json:227855:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-227856-          "statement": "For $M>0$, $|a|<M$, and the Kerr exterior tensor datum, define\nfor $x=(t,r,p)$ the product tangent isomorphism\n$$I_x:T_x\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm K}\\longrightarrow\\mathbb R\\oplus\\mathbb R\\oplus T_pS^2,\\qquad I_x(v):=(dt_x(v),dr_x(v),d\\pi_x(v)).$$\nUsing the sphere rotation field $\\xi$ from the Kerr exterior tensor definition, set\n$T_x:=I_x^{-1}(1,0,0)$ and $\\Phi_x:=I_x^{-1}(0,0,\\xi_p)$. Put\n$A:=r^2+a^2$ and $q:=\\gamma(\\Phi,\\Phi)$.\nThe global vector field\n$$N:=\\frac{A^2-a^2\\Delta q}{\\Sigma\\Delta}\\,T+\\frac{2aMr}{\\Sigma\\Delta}\\,\\Phi$$\nis smooth; the tensor $g$ is smooth, symmetric, nondegenerate, and has\nsignature $(-,+,+,+)$ on all of\n$\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm K}=\\mathbb R\\times(r_+,\\infty)\\times S^2$; and\n$N=-\\sharp_g(dt)$ is timelike. Thus $N$ defines a time orientation of this\nLorentzian four-manifold.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-227857-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-227900-          },
research/plan-spec.json-227901-          "physical_scope": "Conditional mathematical statement about affine geodesics of a metric-selected connection; no physical trajectory or observation is asserted.",
research/plan-spec.json:227902:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-227903-          "statement": "Let $(\\mathcal M,g)$ be a smooth Lorentzian four-manifold, with no global\ntime orientation assumed, and let $\\nabla$ be its metric-selected connection,\nnamely the unique torsion-free affine connection with $\\nabla g=0$.\nLet $K$ be a smooth symmetric covariant $2$-tensor satisfying\n$\\nabla_{(a}K_{bc)}:=(\\nabla_aK_{bc}+\\nabla_bK_{ca}+\\nabla_cK_{ab})/3=0$.\nHere a **rank-two Killing tensor** means precisely such a $K$; this extends\nthe time-oriented definition by the same tensor equation. If\n$\\gamma:I\\to\\mathcal M$ is an affinely parametrized geodesic on a connected\nopen interval $I$, with tangent $v=\\dot\\gamma$, then\n\n$$\\lambda\\longmapsto K_{ab}(\\gamma(\\lambda))v^a(\\lambda)v^b(\\lambda)$$\n\nis constant on $I$.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-227904-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-227953-          },
research/plan-spec.json-227954-          "physical_scope": "Geometric properties of the subextremal Kerr exterior and its regular horizon extension; no black-hole uniqueness or observational claim is made.",
research/plan-spec.json:227955:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-227956-          "statement": "Let $T$ and $\\Phi$ be the stationary and axial product lifts defined in\nthe Kerr exterior metric-properties lemma: for $x=(t,r,p)$,\n$I_x(v)=(dt_x(v),dr_x(v),d\\pi_x(v))$ and\n$T_x=I_x^{-1}(1,0,0)$, $\\Phi_x=I_x^{-1}(0,0,\\xi_p)$, where $\\xi$ is the\nrotation field on $S^2$ from the Kerr exterior tensor definition. Both are Killing\nfields.\nIn a smooth ingoing extension across $r=r_+$, the hypersurface $H^+=\\{r=r_+\\}$\nis null and its null normal direction is generated by\n$\\chi=T+\\Omega_H\\Phi$, where\n$\\Omega_H=a/(r_+^2+a^2)$. In the ingoing product coordinates $(v,r,p)$, the smooth field\n$$\\overline N:=\\partial_v-\\frac{2Mr}{\\Sigma}\\partial_r$$\nis timelike on the extension and selects a time orientation agreeing with the\nchosen exterior time orientation. On $H^+$ one has $g(\\chi,\\overline N)=-1$,\nso $\\chi$ is its future null generator. On the exterior polar chart, $T$ is spacelike\nexactly for\n\n$$r_+<r<r_{\\mathrm s}(\\theta),\\qquad r_{\\mathrm s}(\\theta):=M+\\sqrt{M^2-a^2\\cos^2\\theta}.$$\n\nAt the rotation axis $r_{\\mathrm s}=r_+$, so the open ergoregion has zero\nradial width there.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-227957-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-228002-          },
research/plan-spec.json-228003-          "physical_scope": "A local tensor identity for the specified metric; it does not assert that arbitrary stationary vacuum data are Kerr or that this metric describes nature.",
research/plan-spec.json:228004:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-228005-          "statement": "For the specified Kerr exterior metric $g$, with $M>0$, $|a|<M$, and\n$r>r_+$, the Ricci tensor of its metric-selected connection vanishes:\n$\\operatorname{Ric}(g)=0$. This is a local geometric identity on the entire\nsubextremal exterior, including the rotation axis by smooth extension.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-228006-          "provenance": {
