research/plan-spec.json-229131-          "statement": "For a diagonal Bianchi I datum, write $H_\\Sigma:=H_1+H_2+H_3=3H$. In every local quotient chart, the only nonzero Christoffel symbols are $\\Gamma^0{}_{ii}=a_i^2H_i/c^2$ and $\\Gamma^i{}_{0i}=\\Gamma^i{}_{i0}=H_i$. The possibly nonzero lowered curvature components are exactly those obtained from the following values by the displayed sign reversals:\n\n$$R_{0i0i}=R_{i0i0}=-a_i^2(\\dot H_i+H_i^2),\\qquad R_{0ii0}=R_{i00i}=a_i^2(\\dot H_i+H_i^2),$$\n\n$$R_{ijij}=R_{jiji}=\\frac{a_i^2a_j^2}{c^2}H_iH_j,\\qquad R_{ijji}=R_{jiij}=-\\frac{a_i^2a_j^2}{c^2}H_iH_j\\quad(1\\le i<j\\le3).$$\n\nThe Ricci components are\n\n$$\\operatorname{Ric}_{00}=-\\sum_{i=1}^3(\\dot H_i+H_i^2),\\qquad \\operatorname{Ric}_{ii}=\\frac{a_i^2}{c^2}(\\dot H_i+H_iH_\\Sigma),$$\n\nand every off-diagonal Ricci component is zero.",
