research/plan-spec.json-229173-          "statement": "Let $a_i(t)=A_i(t/t_0)^{p_i}$ on a nonempty open interval $I\\subseteq(0,\\infty)$, where $A_i>0$ are lengths in metres, $t_0>0$ is a time in seconds, and $p_i\\in\\mathbb R$ are dimensionless exponents. These $p_i$ are called Kasner exponents for this power-law branch; define their sums $P:=\\sum_{i=1}^3p_i$ and $Q:=\\sum_{i=1}^3p_i^2$. For a nonstatic datum, meaning that not all $p_i$ vanish, the geometric vacuum equation $\\operatorname{Ric}=0$ in the $C^2$ curvature definition of this page holds exactly when $P=Q=1$. If all $p_i=0$, then the full curvature tensor vanishes, so the metric is flat in the curvature sense. These are exact statements about the specified finite-dimensional metrics; no singularity or generic cosmological conclusion follows.",
research/plan-spec.json-229174-          "strategy": "direct",
