research/plan-spec.json-229212-          "statement": "For a diagonal Bianchi I datum, let $\\Lambda$ be a constant in $\\mathrm{m}^{-2}$ and let $Q_i:I\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuous functions in $\\mathrm{m}^{-2}$. Suppose the spatial diagonal equations\n\n$$G^i{}_i+\\Lambda=Q_i(t)\\qquad(i=1,2,3;\\ \\text{no sum over }i)$$\n\nhold, where $G^i{}_i$ is defined by the local $C^2$ curvature convention on this page. With $\\Delta_{ij}:=H_i-H_j$ and $H_\\Sigma:=3H$, subtracting the equations gives\n\n$$\\dot\\Delta_{ij}+3H\\Delta_{ij}=c^2\\bigl(Q_i-Q_j\\bigr).$$\n\nIf the diagonal source is isotropic, meaning $Q_1=Q_2=Q_3$, then $V\\Delta_{ij}$ is constant for each pair, and there is a constant $C\\ge0$ with units $\\mathrm{m}^6\\mathrm{s}^{-2}$ such that $\\sigma^2=C\\,V^{-2}$ throughout $I$. For unequal diagonal sources the right-hand side remains; this proposition makes no unsourced $V^{-2}$ claim in that case.",
