research/plan-spec.json-229268-          "statement": "On any nonempty open interval $I\\subseteq(0,\\infty)$, the exponents $(p_1,p_2,p_3)=(-1/3,2/3,2/3)$ with $a_i=A_i(t/t_0)^{p_i}$, $A_i>0$ lengths in metres and $t_0>0$ a time in seconds, give a nonstatic Ricci-flat diagonal Bianchi I metric. Its directional expansion rates are unequal, the scalar $\\sigma^2:=\\frac12\\sum_i(H_i-H)^2$ equals $1/(3t^2)$, and its curvature component $R_{0101}=-4a_1^2/(9t^2)$ is nonzero. Thus the Riemann tensor is nonzero and the metric is not flat.\n\n",
