research/plan-spec.json-229309-          "statement": "For lengths $A_i>0$ in metres and a time $t_0>0$ in seconds, set $I=(0,\\infty)$ and take the exponents $(p_1,p_2,p_3)=(1,0,0)$, so $a_1=A_1(t/t_0)$ and $a_2=A_2$, $a_3=A_3$. They satisfy $\\sum_i p_i=1$ and $\\sum_i p_i^2=1$, and the corresponding diagonal Bianchi I metric is Ricci-flat with identically zero Riemann tensor on $I$. Define the open coordinate domain $\\mathcal D:=\\{(T,X,z_2,z_3)\\in\\mathbb R^4:T>|X|\\}$ and its Minkowski metric $\\eta:=-dT^2+dX^2+dz_2^2+dz_3^2$, with all four coordinates measured in metres. In any local quotient chart with lifted dimensionless angular coordinates $x^1,x^2,x^3$, let $\\alpha:=A_1/(ct_0)$ and define\n\n$$\\Phi(t,x^1,x^2,x^3):=(ct\\cosh(\\alpha x^1),\\;ct\\sinh(\\alpha x^1),\\;A_2x^2,\\;A_3x^3).$$\n\nThis map is a local isometry from the chart domain, with the Bianchi I metric, onto an open subset of $(\\mathcal D,\\eta)$. Its scale factor $a_1$ tends to zero as $t\\downarrow0$, but that excluded coordinate boundary alone does not establish curvature blowup or a global extension on the torus quotient.\n\n",
