research/plan-spec.json-230099-          "statement": "For a fixed smooth two-parameter family of commuting variations, replace the\nLagrangian and its selected potential by\n\n$$\\mathcal L'=\\mathcal L+d_M\\mu,\\qquad \\theta'(\\phi;\\delta\\phi) =\\theta(\\phi;\\delta\\phi)+\\delta\\mu(\\phi;\\delta\\phi) +d_MY(\\phi;\\delta\\phi),$$\n\nwhere $\\mu$ is a smooth local spacetime three-form and $Y(\\phi;\\delta\\phi)$\nis a smooth local spacetime two-form, linear in the variation and its\nspacetime derivatives. Their local coefficients depend smoothly on the spacetime coordinates,\nfinitely many derivatives of $\\phi$ and any fixed smooth background fields, and $Y$\ndepends linearly on finitely many derivatives of $\\delta\\phi$. Then\n\n$$\\omega'-\\omega =d_M\\bigl(\\delta_2Y(\\delta_1\\phi)-\\delta_1Y(\\delta_2\\phi)\\bigr).$$\n\nConsequently, for a finite oriented smooth singular three-chain $\\Sigma$,\nthe integrated form changes by the integral of this two-form over\n$\\partial\\Sigma$.",
--
