research/plan-spec.json-230985-          "statement": "Let $K$ be a finite connected CW complex, let $v_0$ be a vertex, and let $T$ be a maximal tree in its 1-skeleton. Choose one orientation of each 1-cell outside $T$. For each such edge $e:u\\to v$, let $x_e$ be the based loop that follows $T$ from $v_0$ to $u$, traverses $e$, and returns along $T$ from $v$ to $v_0$. For every 2-cell $f$, choose a point on its attaching circle and a path in the 1-skeleton from $v_0$ to its image; the resulting based attaching loop has a unique reduced word $r_f$ in the free basis $(x_e)$. Then\n\n$$\\pi_1(K,v_0)\\cong \\langle x_e\\ (e\\notin T)\\mid r_f\\ (f\\text{ a 2-cell})\\rangle.$$\n\nCells of dimension at least three add no generators or relators. Changing the connecting path conjugates its relator, and reversing an edge orientation inverts the corresponding generator, so these choices do not change the presented group.\n\n",
