research/plan-spec.json-231031-          "statement": "Let $M$ be a smooth manifold and $U\\subseteq M$ open. A **piecewise-smooth path** in $U$ is a continuous map $\\gamma:[0,1]\\to U$ for which some finite partition $0=t_0<t_1<\\cdots<t_n=1$ makes every restriction $\\gamma|_{[t_{j-1},t_j]}$ smooth as a map of manifolds with boundary. Its source and target are $\\gamma(0)$ and $\\gamma(1)$. The collection of all such paths is a set: it is a subset, defined by separation, of the function set from $[0,1]$ to $U$.\n\nTwo paths $\\gamma_0,\\gamma_1$ with the same source $x$ and target $y$ are **thin-homotopic**, written $\\gamma_0\\sim_{\\mathrm{thin}}\\gamma_1$, if there is a continuous map $H:[0,1]^2\\to U$ and a finite subdivision of the square into compact curvilinear triangles such that $H$ is smooth up to each triangle's boundary, $H(0,t)=\\gamma_0(t)$, $H(1,t)=\\gamma_1(t)$, $H(s,0)=x$, $H(s,1)=y$, and $\\operatorname{rank}(dH_{(s,t)})\\le 1$ on every smooth triangle. A **curvilinear triangle** here is a compact region $D$ equipped with a specified homeomorphism $\\psi:\\Delta^2\\to D$ from the standard closed two-simplex which is a smooth embedding on the interior, extends smoothly to a neighborhood of $\\Delta^2$ in its affine span, and maps the three edges of $\\Delta^2$ to the three boundary arcs of $D$. Saying $H$ is smooth up to $D$'s boundary means that $H\\circ\\psi$ extends smoothly from $\\Delta^2$ to an open neighborhood of $\\Delta^2$ in its affine span, with values in $U$; equivalently, it is a smooth singular $2$-simplex under the neighborhood-extension convention of [[def-smooth-singular-simplex]]. The rank is the dimension of the image of the differential from the two-dimensional tangent space of the triangle to $T_{H(s,t)}M$, computed through the interior chart $\\psi$ and extended to boundary points by these smooth extensions. The quotient by this relation is used only after its equivalence and compatibility properties are proved.\n\n",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231065-            "def-isomorphism-groupoid-and-connected-category": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231066-          },
