research/plan-spec.json-231191-          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$ and let $0=t_0<t_1<\\cdots<t_m=1$ be a finite partition. For each $j$, let $A_j:[t_{j-1},t_j]\\to M_n(\\mathbb R)$ be continuous. There is a unique continuous function $U:[0,1]\\to M_n(\\mathbb R)$ that is $C^1$ on each partition interval, satisfies $U'(t)=-A_j(t)U(t)$ in its interior, and has $U(0)=I_n$. Derivatives at interval endpoints are the corresponding one-sided derivatives.",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231230-            "def-gauge-group-of-a-smooth-principal-bundle": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231231-          },
research/plan-spec.json:231232:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
