research/plan-spec.json-231380-          "dependency_level": 4,
research/plan-spec.json-231381-          "statement": "Fix coordinate dimension $n\\ge2$ and matrix size $q\\ge1$, independently. Let $V\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be an open coordinate domain, let $K\\subset V$ be compact with positive distance from $\\mathbb R^n\\setminus V$, and let $e_1,\\ldots,e_n$ be the standard basis of $\\mathbb R^n$. Let $\\omega=\\sum_{k=1}^n\\omega_k(x)\\,dx^k$ be a $C^2$ $M_q(\\mathbb R)$-valued connection one-form, with each $\\omega_k:V\\to M_q(\\mathbb R)$. Along each segment use the matrix ODE $U'=-\\omega(\\dot\\gamma)U$ and initial value $I_q$; existence and uniqueness for this fixed matrix size follow from [[prop-gr-fx-connection-path-transport-exists]]. For the tetrad connection of [[def-gr-fx-connection-path-transport]], take $q=4$. For $p\\in K$, distinct coordinate directions $i,j$, and sufficiently small positive $\\varepsilon$ so the square stays in $V$, define $\\gamma_\\varepsilon$ by traversing each straight side at constant speed over one quarter of $[0,1]$, in the order\n\n$$p\\to p+\\varepsilon e_i\\to p+\\varepsilon e_i+\\varepsilon e_j\\to p+\\varepsilon e_j\\to p.$$\n\nIts boundary orientation is positive for the ordered coordinate pair $(e_i,e_j)$.\n\n$$U_{\\gamma_\\varepsilon}(1)=I_q-\\varepsilon^2F_{ij}(p)+O(\\varepsilon^3),\\qquad F_{ij}=\\partial_i\\omega_j-\\partial_j\\omega_i+[\\omega_i,\\omega_j]\\in M_q(\\mathbb R).$$\n\nHere $I_q$ is the identity in $M_q(\\mathbb R)$ and fix a norm $\\|\\cdot\\|$ on that space satisfying $\\|AB\\|\\le\\|A\\|\\,\\|B\\|$ for all $A,B\\in M_q(\\mathbb R)$. The notation $O(\\varepsilon^3)$ means that the norm of the remainder is at most $C\\varepsilon^3$ for all sufficiently small positive $\\varepsilon$, with $C$ uniform for basepoints $p\\in K$.\n\n",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231422-            "def-topological-group": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231423-          },
research/plan-spec.json:231424:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-231425-          "dependency_level": 0,
research/plan-spec.json-231426-          "statement": "Let $M_2(\\mathbb C)$ have its Euclidean topology as $\\mathbb R^8$, write $Q^\\dagger:=\\overline Q^{\\mathsf T}$ for conjugate transpose, and define\n\n$$SU(2)=\\{Q\\in M_2(\\mathbb C):Q^\\dagger Q=I_2,\\ \\det Q=1\\}.$$\n\nUnder matrix multiplication, $SU(2)$ is a compact Hausdorff topological group.\n\n",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231467-            "def-trace-of-an-endomorphism": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231468-          },
research/plan-spec.json:231469:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-231470-          "dependency_level": 1,
research/plan-spec.json-231471-          "statement": "A **finite oriented graph** consists of finite vertex and edge sets $V,E$, source and target maps $s,t:E\\to V$, and a fixed-point-free involution $e\\mapsto\\bar e$ with $s(\\bar e)=t(e)$ and $t(\\bar e)=s(e)$. A **finite SU(2) graph configuration** assigns $g_e\\in SU(2)$ to every oriented edge and requires $g_{\\bar e}=g_e^{-1}$. A graph path is a finite composable edge word $e_1,\\ldots,e_n$; its holonomy is the later-left product $g_{e_n}\\cdots g_{e_1}$, and the empty path has holonomy $I_2$.\n\nA vertex gauge assignment is a function $h:V\\to SU(2)$. It acts on edge variables by\n\n$$g_e\\longmapsto g'_e=h_{t(e)}g_eh_{s(e)}^{-1}.$$\n\nA **finite-dimensional unitary representation** is a group homomorphism $\\rho:SU(2)\\to U(W)$ on a finite-dimensional complex inner-product space $W$ that is strongly continuous, meaning $g\\mapsto\\rho(g)w$ is continuous for each $w\\in W$. Here\n\n$$U(W):=\\{T\\in\\operatorname{GL}(W):\\langle Tv,Tw\\rangle=\\langle v,w\\rangle\\text{ for all }v,w\\in W\\},$$\n\nwith the operator-norm topology inherited from $\\operatorname{End}(W)$. In finite dimension, strong continuity is equivalent to continuity in this operator norm.\n\nFor a closed graph path $\\ell=(e_1,\\ldots,e_n)$, the associated **Wilson trace** is the basis-independent trace of the endomorphism of $W$ given by\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\rho(g_{e_n})\\cdots\\rho(g_{e_1})\\bigr).$$\n\nHere the trace of a finite-dimensional endomorphism is the trace of its matrix in any basis.\n\n",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231504-            "def-gr-fx-discrete-holonomy-model": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231505-          },
research/plan-spec.json:231506:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-231507-          "dependency_level": 2,
research/plan-spec.json-231508-          "statement": "For every finite SU(2) graph configuration, continuous finite-dimensional unitary representation $\\rho$, closed graph path $\\ell$, and vertex gauge assignment $h$, the Wilson trace of $\\ell$ is unchanged by $g_e\\mapsto h_{t(e)}g_eh_{s(e)}^{-1}$.",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231565-            "def-orthogonal-projection": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231566-          },
research/plan-spec.json:231567:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-231568-          "dependency_level": 2,
research/plan-spec.json-231569-          "statement": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let a finite oriented graph be given, fix total orders on its finite vertex and edge sets, and for each edge $e$ choose a finite-dimensional strongly continuous unitary representation $\\rho_e:SU(2)\\to U(V_e)$. At a vertex $v$ set\n\n$$W_v=\\bigotimes_{t(e)=v}V_e\\;\\otimes\\!\\bigotimes_{s(e)=v}V_e^*,$$\n\nwhere the edge order induces the order on each factor list and an empty tensor product is $\\mathbb C$. Use the dual action $g\\cdot\\lambda=\\lambda\\circ\\rho_e(g^{-1})$ on $V_e^*$, with the dual Hilbert inner product determined by any orthonormal basis of $V_e$. On elementary tensors use the tensor-product inner product $\\langle\\bigotimes_i u_i,\\bigotimes_i w_i\\rangle=\\prod_i\\langle u_i,w_i\\rangle$, extended sesquilinearly. Let $R_v$ be the resulting diagonal unitary representation and define its fixed-vector subspace by\n\n$$W_v^{SU(2)}:=\\{w\\in W_v:R_v(g)w=w\\text{ for every }g\\in SU(2)\\}.$$\n\nAn orthogonal projection onto a subspace $S\\subseteq W_v$, regarded as an endomorphism of $W_v$, is the idempotent with range $S$ and kernel $S^\\perp$.\n\nFor the normalized Haar probability measure $\\mu$ on $SU(2)$,\n\n$$P_vw:=\\int_{SU(2)}R_v(g)w\\,d\\mu(g)$$\n\nis the orthogonal projection of $W_v$ onto its invariant subspace $W_v^{SU(2)}$. The vector integral is defined coordinatewise in the finite-dimensional space, equivalently by the weak integral in [[def-haar-averaging-operator-on-hom-spaces]]. On the coefficient space $W=\\bigotimes_{v\\in V}W_v$, with vertex order fixed as above, the operators $P_v$ acting on their respective vertex factors commute, and $\\prod_{v\\in V}P_v$ projects onto the tensors invariant at every vertex. This is a finite kinematic projection; it imposes no Hamiltonian or continuum constraint.\n\n",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231633-            "prop-pullback-of-forms-is-smooth-functorial-and-preserves-wedges": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231634-          },
research/plan-spec.json:231635:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-231636-          "dependency_level": 4,
research/plan-spec.json-231637-          "statement": "Let $M=S^1\\times\\mathbb R^3$, write $(x,y)$ for the standard embedding coordinates on $S^1$, and set $\\alpha=x\\,dy-y\\,dx$. With real coordinates $t,z_1,z_2$ on $\\mathbb R^3$, define\n\n$$g=-dt\\otimes dt+\\alpha\\otimes\\alpha+dz_1\\otimes dz_1+dz_2\\otimes dz_2.$$\n\nThe global frame $E_0=\\partial_t$, $E_1=-y\\partial_x+x\\partial_y$, $E_2=\\partial_{z_1}$, $E_3=\\partial_{z_2}$ is an orthonormal tetrad for $g$ with signature $(-,+,+,+)$. Here $E_1$ is the restriction of the indicated ambient vector field to $S^1$, where it is tangent because it is orthogonal to $(x,y)$. Orient $M$ by this ordered frame and time-orient it by $E_0$. Let $J$ be the constant matrix with $JE_2=E_3$, $JE_3=-E_2$, and $JE_0=JE_1=0$. Assume the $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ convention in [[def-gr-fx-tetrad-spin-connection]]. Define $\\omega=\\tfrac14J\\alpha$ and the affine connection on this frame by\n\n$$\\nabla_X\\Bigl(\\sum_Jv^J E_J\\Bigr):=\\sum_I\\Bigl(X(v^I)+\\sum_J\\omega^I{}_J(X)v^J\\Bigr)E_I.$$\n\nFor a real $4\\times4$ matrix $A$, $\\exp(A)$ denotes the matrix series $\\sum_{m=0}^\\infty A^m/m!$, which converges absolutely in any fixed submultiplicative matrix norm.\n\nThis is a flat Lorentz connection. On any coordinate arc of $S^1$ with angular coordinate $\\theta$, transport between endpoints is $\\exp(-\\tfrac14J(\\theta_1-\\theta_0))$, independent of the chosen path inside that arc. Around the once-around loop it is $\\exp(-\\tfrac\\pi2J)\\ne I_4$, although the curvature is zero; the loop is not thin-contractible.\n\n",
--
research/plan-spec.json-231674-            "prop-gr-fx-su2-compact": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-231675-          },
