research/plan-spec.json-232235-          "statement": "Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space and let $T:D(T)\\to H$ be a densely defined symmetric linear operator. The false assertion is that there is a self-adjoint operator $A:D(A)\\to H$ on the same Hilbert space with $D(T)\\subseteq D(A)$ and $Af=Tf$ for every $f\\in D(T)$. By Stone's theorem, such an $A$ would generate a strongly continuous one-parameter unitary group $U(t)=e^{itA}$ on $H$.",
research/plan-spec.json-232236-          "justified_by": [],
