research/plan-spec.json-233223-          "statement": "Let $I$ be an open energy interval and let $\\delta:I\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^1$. The one-channel unitary matrix $S(E)=e^{2i\\delta(E)}\\in U(1)$ has Wigner–Smith matrix $Q(E)=2\\hbar\\,\\delta'(E)$, which is real and has units of seconds when $E$ is measured in joules and $\\hbar$ in joule-seconds. This algebraic quantity is not, without further model assumptions, an operational arrival-time measurement.",
