research/plan-spec.json:235270:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-235271-          "statement": "For an integer $d\\ge1$, let $\\mathsf H_d=\\{A\\in M_d(\\mathbb C):A=A^*\\}$, regarded as a real vector space. For $A,B\\in\\mathsf H_d$, define the trace pairing $\\langle A,B\\rangle_{\\mathrm{HS}}:=\\operatorname{Tr}(AB)$ and write $\\|A\\|_{\\mathrm{HS}}:=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{Tr}(A^2)}$. The following A-page lemma verifies that the pairing is a real inner product and that this expression is its norm.\n\nLet $m\\ge1$ and let $F=(F_a)_{a=1}^m$ be a finite family in $\\mathsf H_d$. It is informationally complete when its real linear span is all of $\\mathsf H_d$. Its synthesis map is $S:\\mathbb R^m\\to\\mathsf H_d$, $S c=\\sum_{a=1}^m c_aF_a$. Define the Gram matrix by $G_{ab}:=\\operatorname{Tr}(F_aF_b)$.\n\nEquip $\\mathbb R^m$ with the dot product $c^\\mathsf Tb=\\sum_{a=1}^m c_ab_a$. Here $S^*:\\mathsf H_d\\to\\mathbb R^m$ denotes the adjoint relative to this dot product and the displayed trace pairing: it is characterized by $c^\\mathsf T(S^*X)=\\langle Sc,X\\rangle_{\\mathrm{HS}}$ for every $c\\in\\mathbb R^m$ and $X\\in\\mathsf H_d$. The following lemma proves that the trace pairing is an inner product and that this adjoint exists as a well-defined linear map; it also establishes that $G=S^*S$ is real symmetric positive semidefinite.\n\nFor this positive semidefinite real matrix $G$, let $G^+$ be its unique Moore–Penrose pseudoinverse in $M_m(\\mathbb R)$, defined by the four Penrose equations over $\\mathbb R$. Define the canonical dual operators $D_a=\\sum_{b=1}^m(G^+)_{ba}F_b$ and the reconstruction map $D:\\mathbb R^m\\to\\mathsf H_d$, $D c=\\sum_{a=1}^m c_aD_a$. A later A-page lemma identifies this finite pseudoinverse with its spectral formula.",
research/plan-spec.json-235272-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-235305-            "lem-bounded-variable-hoeffding-mgf": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-235306-          },
