research/plan-spec.json-235488-          "statement": "Let $d,m\\ge1$, let $F_1,\\ldots,F_m\\in\\mathsf H_d$ span $\\mathsf H_d$ over $\\mathbb R$, and form $S$, $G=S^*S$, $G^+$, and $D_a$ as in the preceding finite-frame definition. If $G=\\sum_{\\lambda>0}\\lambda P_\\lambda$ is its finite spectral resolution, then $G^+=\\sum_{\\lambda>0}\\lambda^{-1}P_\\lambda$. Moreover, every $X\\in\\mathsf H_d$ is reconstructed by\n$$\nX=\\sum_{a=1}^m\\operatorname{Tr}(XF_a)D_a.\n$$\nThis holds for redundant families as well as bases; $G$ need not be invertible.",
research/plan-spec.json-235489-          "provenance": {
