research/plan-spec.json-238104-            "lem-nrqmx-finite-hermitian-matrix-exponential": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-238105-          },
research/plan-spec.json:238106:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-238107-          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\ge1$, $T>0$, $\\hbar>0$, $\\omega=2\\pi/T$, and let $H:\\mathbb R\\to M_d(\\mathbb C)$ be continuous, $T$-periodic, and Hermitian at every time. Let $U(t,s)$ be the unitary propagator solving $i\\hbar\\,\\partial_tU(t,s)=H(t)U(t,s)$ and $U(s,s)=I_d$. There are an orthonormal basis $v_1,\\ldots,v_d$ and real numbers $\\varepsilon_1,\\ldots,\\varepsilon_d$ such that\n$$U(T,0)v_j=e^{-iT\\varepsilon_j/\\hbar}v_j\\qquad(1\\le j\\le d).$$\nDefine the Hermitian matrix $H_Fv_j=\\varepsilon_jv_j$ and the quasienergy classes $\\varepsilon_j+\\hbar\\omega\\mathbb Z$. With $P(t):=U(t,0)e^{itH_F/\\hbar}$, $P(t)$ is a $T$-periodic unitary matrix and\n$$U(t,0)=P(t)e^{-itH_F/\\hbar}\\qquad(t\\in\\mathbb R).$$\nThe real representative $\\varepsilon_j$ may be changed by any integer multiple of $\\hbar\\omega$ without changing its eigenphase; no preferred real branch is asserted.",
research/plan-spec.json-238108-          "justified_by": [],
--
research/plan-spec.json-238164-            "lem-bochner-integral-norm-inequality": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-238165-          },
