research/plan-spec.json-238693-          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $H\\ne\\{0\\}$ be a complex Hilbert space, let $T=T^*$ be self-adjoint on $H$, and fix $\\hbar>0$. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval, let $t_0\\in I$, and let $v\\in C^1(I;H)$ satisfy $v(s)\\in D(T)$ for every $s\\in I$ and $s\\mapsto Tv(s)$ continuous. Define $r(s)=i\\hbar v'(s)-Tv(s)$ and $U_T(t,t_0)=e^{-i(t-t_0)T/\\hbar}$ by the Borel functional calculus. Then for every $t\\in I$,\n\n$$\\|v(t)-U_T(t,t_0)v(t_0)\\|\\le\\frac1\\hbar\\int_{\\min(t,t_0)}^{\\max(t,t_0)}\\|r(s)\\|\\,ds.$$\n\nThe integral is the ordinary integral of the continuous real-valued function $s\\mapsto\\|r(s)\\|$; the bound is conditional on the stated operator-domain regularity and makes no assertion about an asymptotic approximation outside this residual estimate.",
research/plan-spec.json-238694-          "justified_by": [],
