research/plan-spec.json-239132-          "statement": "In the resonant Jaynes–Cummings model ($\\omega_0=\\omega$), prepare the atom and field in $|e,0\\rangle$ and let the ideal model evolve for time $\\tau\\ge0$. The assigned excited-state PVM then gives excitation probability $\\cos^2(g\\tau)$. If $g\\ne0$, the population returns to one at $\\tau=k\\pi/|g|$, $k\\in\\mathbb N_0$; if $g=0$, it remains one. This is a periodic model prediction, not irreversible spontaneous decay or a reported observation.",
research/plan-spec.json-239133-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-239174-            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-239175-          },
