research/plan-spec.json-243369-          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $(X,Y)$ have a centered, possibly degenerate, jointly Gaussian law with covariance matrix $\\begin{pmatrix}\\sigma^2&c\\\\c&\\tau^2\\end{pmatrix}$, where $\\sigma^2,\\tau^2\\ge0$ and the matrix is positive semidefinite. Define $:X^n:_{\\sigma^2}$ and $:Y^m:_{\\tau^2}$ by the finite covariance Wick-power generating identity. For all integers $n,m\\ge0$,\n\n$$\\mathbb E\\bigl[:X^n:_{\\sigma^2}:Y^m:_{\\tau^2}\\bigr]=\\begin{cases}n!c^n,&n=m,\\\\0,&n\\ne m,\\end{cases}$$\n\nwith $c^0:=1$.",
research/plan-spec.json:243370:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-243371-          "proof_strategy": "direct"
