research/plan-spec.json-243413-          },
research/plan-spec.json-243414-          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice, its countable-family consequence, and $m>0$. Let $\\Phi$ be the real centered Gaussian random tempered distribution on $\\mathbb R^2$ with covariance $C_m(f,g)=(2\\pi)^{-2}\\int_{\\mathbb R^2}\\overline{\\widehat f(p)}\\widehat g(p)(|p|^2+m^2)^{-1}\\,d^2p$ for real Schwartz tests and $\\widehat f(p)=\\int e^{-ip\\cdot x}f(x)\\,d^2x$. Write $\\mu_C$ for the Gaussian probability measure on the cylinder $\\sigma$-algebra of $\\mathcal S'_\\mathbb R(\\mathbb R^2)$ supplied by [[thm-qftx-tempered-massive-gaussian-field]], equivalently the law of $\\Phi$; all expectations below are with respect to $\\mu_C$. Fix one nonnegative $\\rho\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^2)$ with $\\int\\rho(x)\\,d^2x=1$, set $\\rho_\\epsilon(x)=\\epsilon^{-2}\\rho(x/\\epsilon)$ for $\\epsilon>0$, and define $\\Phi_\\epsilon(x)=\\Phi(u\\mapsto\\rho_\\epsilon(x-u))$. For each $n\\ge0$, define the finite-cutoff Wick polynomial $:\\!\\Phi_\\epsilon(x)^n\\!:$ by\n\n$$\\exp\\!\\left(t\\Phi_\\epsilon(x)-\\tfrac12t^2\\mathbb E[\\Phi_\\epsilon(x)^2]\\right)=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}:\\!\\Phi_\\epsilon(x)^n\\!:\\,\\frac{t^n}{n!}$$\n\nas an identity of formal power series. For a bounded measurable $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb C$ that vanishes outside a bounded set, define its cutoff smearing by the samplewise Lebesgue integral $W_{\\epsilon,n}(f)=\\int f(x):\\!\\Phi_\\epsilon(x)^n\\!:\\,d^2x$. Every tempered sample gives a smooth $x\\mapsto\\Phi_\\epsilon(x)$, so this integral is finite for each sample; its $L^2(\\mu_C)$ limit as $\\epsilon\\downarrow0$ is a separate theorem, not part of this definition.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json:243415:          "inventory_expansion_required": false
