research/plan-spec.json-245114-            "thm-closed-oriented-two-dimensional-tqfts-are-commutative-frobenius-algebras": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-245115-          },
research/plan-spec.json:245116:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-245117-          "statement": "Fix an integer $r\\ge1$ and let $A=\\bigoplus_{i=1}^{r}\\mathbb C e_i$, with coordinatewise multiplication $e_i e_j=\\delta_{ij}e_i$ and unit $1_A=\\sum_{i=1}^{r}e_i$. Choose weights $w_i\\in\\mathbb C^\\times$ and define $\\epsilon(e_i)=w_i$ and $\\Delta(e_i)=w_i^{-1}e_i\\otimes e_i$. The Frobenius pairing $b(a,b)=\\epsilon(ab)$ is diagonal in the basis $(e_i)$ with entries $w_i$; $\\Delta$ is the inverse-pairing comultiplication. These maps define a finite-dimensional commutative Frobenius algebra over $\\mathbb C$.\n\nA **closed oriented two-dimensional TQFT** here is a strong symmetric monoidal functor from $\\mathsf{Cob}^{\\mathrm{cl}}_2$ to $\\mathrm{Vect}_{\\mathrm{fd}}(\\mathbb C)$. The objects of $\\mathsf{Cob}^{\\mathrm{cl}}_2$ are finite ordered words of oriented circles; its morphisms are compact oriented smooth surfaces with parametrized incoming and outgoing circle boundaries and no free boundary, modulo orientation-preserving diffeomorphism relative to those boundary parameterizations. Composition is collar gluing and the monoidal operation is ordered disjoint union. The supplied closed classification associates to $(A,\\mu,\\eta,\\Delta,\\epsilon)$ a closed oriented two-dimensional TQFT. Put $H=\\mu\\circ\\Delta$. For the connected closed surface $\\Sigma_g$ of genus $g\\ge0$, it assigns $Z_A(\\Sigma_g)=\\epsilon(H^g(\\eta(1)))$; the cylinder acts by $1_A$.\n\nThis is a closed-sector construction. It asserts no open sector, Cardy datum, or fully extended point-level theory. Countable choice is inherited only through the root surface-normal-form input to the classification.",
research/plan-spec.json-245118-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-245158-            "def-qftx-frobenius-semisimple-model": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-245159-          },
research/plan-spec.json:245160:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-245161-          "statement": "For the semisimple closed model defined by the stated idempotent data, let $H=\\mu\\circ\\Delta$ and let $g\\ge0$ be an integer. The connected closed genus-$g$ amplitude is $Z_A(\\Sigma_g)=\\sum_{i=1}^{r}w_i^{1-g}$. The cylinder acts by $1_A$, and the torus amplitude is $r$.",
research/plan-spec.json-245162-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-245202-            "def-qftx-frobenius-semisimple-model": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-245203-          },
research/plan-spec.json:245204:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-245205-          "statement": "For the semisimple closed model determined by the stated idempotent data, define $a^*=\\sum_i\\overline{a_i}e_i$ when $a=\\sum_i a_i e_i$, and set $h(a,b)=\\epsilon(a^*b)$. The form $h$ is a Hermitian positive-definite inner product exactly when every weight $w_i$ is a positive real number. The algebraic closed oriented TQFT exists for every nonzero complex weight; positivity is an additional condition for this specified Hilbert-space interpretation.",
research/plan-spec.json-245206-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-245262-            "thm-closed-oriented-two-dimensional-tqfts-are-commutative-frobenius-algebras": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-245263-          },
research/plan-spec.json:245264:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-245265-          "statement": "Let $A=\\mathbb C[x]/(x^2)$ with basis $(1,x)$, unit $1$, multiplication inherited from the quotient, and Frobenius functional $\\epsilon(1)=0$, $\\epsilon(x)=1$. The bilinear pairing $b(a,b)=\\epsilon(ab)$ has matrix $\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix}$ in that basis, hence is nondegenerate. With the conjugate-linear involution fixing $x$, the form $h(a,b)=\\epsilon(a^*b)$ is Hermitian but indefinite. Here a finite-dimensional algebra is semisimple when its Jacobson radical (the intersection of its maximal left ideals) is zero; $A$ is not semisimple because $x$ is a nonzero nilpotent in that radical. The closed oriented classification therefore gives a closed two-dimensional TQFT from a nonsemisimple Frobenius algebra without asserting positive reflection form data.",
research/plan-spec.json-245266-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-245535-          "justified_by": [],
research/plan-spec.json-245536-          "dependency_roles": {},
research/plan-spec.json:245537:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-245538-          "statement": "A **finite groupoid** is a small category in which every morphism is invertible, with finitely many isomorphism classes and a finite automorphism group at every object. Write $\\pi_0(\\mathcal C)$ for its set of isomorphism classes. Its **groupoid cardinality** is\n\n$$|\\mathcal C|:=\\sum_{[c]\\in\\pi_0(\\mathcal C)}\\frac{1}{|\\operatorname{Aut}_{\\mathcal C}(c)|}.$$\n\nFor an isomorphism-invariant function $f:\\pi_0(\\mathcal C)\\to\\mathbb C$, define\n\n$$\\int_{c\\in\\mathcal C} f(c):=\\sum_{[c]\\in\\pi_0(\\mathcal C)}\\frac{f(c)}{|\\operatorname{Aut}_{\\mathcal C}(c)|}.$$\n\nFor finite groupoids $\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D$, a functor $p:\\mathcal C\\to\\mathcal D$, and an object $d$ of $\\mathcal D$, its **homotopy fiber** $\\mathcal C_d$ has objects $(c,\\alpha)$ with $\\alpha:p(c)\\overset{\\cong}{\\longrightarrow}d$ and morphisms $u:(c,\\alpha)\\to(c',\\alpha')$ satisfying $\\alpha'\\circ p(u)=\\alpha$. Define pullback and pushforward of invariant functions by\n\n$$(p^*g)([c])=g([p(c)]),\\qquad (p_!f)([d])=\\int_{(c,\\alpha)\\in\\mathcal C_d} f([c]).$$\n\nA span $\\mathcal X\\xleftarrow{a}\\mathcal E\\xrightarrow{b}\\mathcal Y$ of finite groupoids therefore induces the linear map $b_!a^*$ on invariant functions.",
research/plan-spec.json-245539-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-245577-            "def-qftx-finite-groupoid-integration": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-245578-          },
research/plan-spec.json:245579:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-245580-          "statement": "Let $p:\\mathcal C\\to\\mathcal D$ and $q:\\mathcal E\\to\\mathcal D$ be functors of finite groupoids. The **homotopy pullback groupoid** $\\mathcal C\\times^h_{\\mathcal D}\\mathcal E$ has objects $(c,e,\\alpha)$, where $c\\in\\mathcal C$, $e\\in\\mathcal E$, and $\\alpha:p(c)\\overset{\\cong}{\\longrightarrow}q(e)$ is an isomorphism in $\\mathcal D$. A morphism $(u,v):(c,e,\\alpha)\\to(c',e',\\alpha')$ consists of isomorphisms $u:c\\to c'$ and $v:e\\to e'$ satisfying\n\n$$q(v)\\circ\\alpha=\\alpha'\\circ p(u).$$\n\nComposition is componentwise. The projections to $\\mathcal C$ and $\\mathcal E$ send $(c,e,\\alpha)$ to $c$ and $e$, respectively.",
research/plan-spec.json-245581-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-245621-            "thm-qftx-cw-fundamental-group-presentation": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-245622-          },
research/plan-spec.json:245623:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-245624-          "statement": "Let $K$ be a finite connected CW complex and $G$ a finite group. Choose an orientation of each 1-cell and, for each 2-cell, its based attaching word in the finite edge presentation of $\\pi_1(K)$; the choice of base paths is part of that presentation. A **flat edge assignment** is a label $g_e\\in G$ for every oriented 1-cell with $g_{\\bar e}=g_e^{-1}$, such that each attaching word has holonomy $1$. If a word traverses edges $e_1,\\ldots,e_m$ in that order with exponents $\\epsilon_j\\in\\{1,-1\\}$, its holonomy is $g_{e_m}^{\\epsilon_m}\\cdots g_{e_1}^{\\epsilon_1}$.\n\nWrite $\\operatorname{Flat}(K,G)$ for the finite set of flat assignments and $K_0$ for the vertices. The finite vertex gauge group $G^{K_0}$ acts by\n\n$$(h\\cdot g)_e=h_{t(e)}g_eh_{s(e)}^{-1},$$\n\nwhere $s(e)$ and $t(e)$ are the source and target vertices. The **finite flat connection groupoid** $\\mathcal C_G(K)$ is the action groupoid $\\operatorname{Flat}(K,G)//G^{K_0}$: its objects are flat assignments and its arrows $g\\to g'$ are the $h\\in G^{K_0}$ with $h\\cdot g=g'$. Its untwisted finite BF partition function is the groupoid cardinality\n\n$$Z_G(K):=|\\mathcal C_G(K)|=\\sum_{[g]\\in\\operatorname{Flat}(K,G)/G^{K_0}}\\frac{1}{|\\operatorname{Stab}(g)|} =\\frac{|\\operatorname{Flat}(K,G)|}{|G|^{|K_0|}}.$$\n\nThis is a finite combinatorial model; it has no continuous Lie-algebra-valued connection integral or additional cocycle phase.\n\nFor a finite disconnected CW complex, define $\\mathcal C_G(K)$ to be the product of the groupoids of its connected components; for the empty complex use the terminal groupoid.",
research/plan-spec.json-245625-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-245675-            "def-qftx-finite-homotopy-pullback": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-245676-          },
