research/plan-spec.json:245832:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-245833-          "statement": "Let $M_1$ and $M_2$ be compact triangulated $d$-bordisms glued along an identified closed triangulated boundary $\\Sigma$, with collars and compatible triangulations. The finite flat-connection groupoid on the glued manifold is equivalent to the homotopy pullback groupoid\n\n$$\\mathcal C_G(M_2\\cup_\\Sigma M_1) \\simeq \\mathcal C_G(M_2)\\times^h_{\\mathcal C_G(\\Sigma)}\\mathcal C_G(M_1).$$\n\nWriting $r_i:\\mathcal C_G(M_i)\\to\\mathcal C_G(\\Sigma)$ for restriction, a pullback object is $(A_2,A_1,\\alpha:r_2(A_2)\\cong r_1(A_1))$. A morphism $(u_2,u_1)$ to $(A_2',A_1',\\alpha')$ satisfies $r_1(u_1)\\circ\\alpha=\\alpha'\\circ r_2(u_2)$.",
research/plan-spec.json-245834-          "provenance": {
