research/plan-spec.json-255931-          },
research/plan-spec.json:255932:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-255933-          "statement": "For the ordered monodromy on $V_N$ with $V=\\mathbb C^2$, define the shifted\nsite operator $L_{aj}(u):=R_{aj}(u-i/2)$, shifted monodromy\n$T_a^L(u):=L_{aN}(u)\\cdots L_{a1}(u)$, and shifted transfer matrix\n$\\tau(u):=\\operatorname{tr}_aT_a^L(u)$. In the ordered auxiliary basis\n$e_\\uparrow,e_\\downarrow$, write\n$$T_a^L(u)=\\begin{pmatrix}A(u)&B(u)\\\\C(u)&D(u)\\end{pmatrix}_a, \\qquad \\Omega:=e_\\uparrow^{\\otimes N}.$$\nFor an integer $M$ with $0\\le M\\le N$, a **regular on-shell Bethe datum** is\na tuple of finite complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_M$ satisfying all\nof the following conditions:\n\n1. The roots are pairwise distinct, none equals $i/2$ or $-i/2$, and no\n   difference $\\lambda_j-\\lambda_k$ for $j\\ne k$ equals $i$ or $-i$.\n2. For each $j=1,\\ldots,M$,\n   $$\\left(\\frac{\\lambda_j+i/2}{\\lambda_j-i/2}\\right)^N =\\prod_{k\\ne j}\\frac{\\lambda_j-\\lambda_k+i}{\\lambda_j-\\lambda_k-i}.$$\n3. The associated vector\n   $$\\Psi(\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_M):= B(\\lambda_1)\\cdots B(\\lambda_M)\\Omega$$\n   is nonzero.\n\nFor $M=0$ the root tuple and products are empty and $\\Psi=\\Omega$. This\ndefinition records regular solutions and nonzero vectors only; it makes no\nclaim of completeness, covers no singular-root regularization, and does not\ninclude descendants generated from other reference vectors.",
research/plan-spec.json-255934-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-255970-            "lem-qsmx-monodromy-rtt": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-255971-          },
research/plan-spec.json:255972:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-255973-          "statement": "Let $V_N=(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes N}$, $N\\ge3$, with auxiliary copy\n$V_a=\\mathbb C^2$, $R_{aj}(u)=uI+iP_{aj}$, where $P_{aj}$ swaps the auxiliary\nfactor with site $j$, and\n$L_{aj}(u)=R_{aj}(u-i/2)$. Define\n$T_a^L(u)=L_{aN}(u)\\cdots L_{a1}(u)$,\n$\\tau(u)=\\operatorname{tr}_aT_a^L(u)$, and the auxiliary entries\n$T_a^L(u)=\\begin{pmatrix}A(u)&B(u)\\\\C(u)&D(u)\\end{pmatrix}_a$ in the ordered\nbasis $e_\\uparrow,e_\\downarrow$. Put $\\Omega=e_\\uparrow^{\\otimes N}$. Suppose\nfinite roots $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_M$, $0\\le M\\le N$, are pairwise\ndistinct, avoid $\\pm i/2$, have no pairwise difference equal to $\\pm i$,\nsatisfy\n$$\\left(\\frac{\\lambda_j+i/2}{\\lambda_j-i/2}\\right)^N =\\prod_{k\\ne j}\\frac{\\lambda_j-\\lambda_k+i}{\\lambda_j-\\lambda_k-i} \\quad(1\\le j\\le M),$$\nand give the nonzero vector $\\Psi=\\prod_{j=1}^M B(\\lambda_j)\\Omega$. For\n$u\\notin\\{\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_M\\}$ its eigenvalue is\n$$\\Lambda(u)=(u+i/2)^N\\prod_{j=1}^M\\frac{u-\\lambda_j-i}{u-\\lambda_j} +(u-i/2)^N\\prod_{j=1}^M\\frac{u-\\lambda_j+i}{u-\\lambda_j}.$$\nThe apparent poles cancel, so $\\Lambda$ extends to a polynomial and the\neigenvector identity holds for every $u\\in\\mathbb C$. This result asserts no\nconverse, singular-root regularization, descendant construction, or completeness.",
research/plan-spec.json-255974-          "provenance": {
