research/plan-spec.json:256140:          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
research/plan-spec.json-256141-          "statement": "For $Q\\in\\{2,3,4\\}$, $L\\geq1$, real coefficients $J_i$, and finite real $\\beta$, the matrix $H_{Q,L}(\\mathbf J)$ defined on the Potts-clock chain is self-adjoint. With the spectral definitions $B_\\beta$, $Z_\\beta$, and $\\rho_\\beta$ from that definition, $Z_\\beta>0$ and $\\rho_\\beta$ is a positive semidefinite matrix of trace one. This is a finite-dimensional mathematical fact; it makes no thermodynamic-limit or empirical claim.",
research/plan-spec.json-256142-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-256184-            "thm-the-symmetric-group-has-the-coxeter-presentation": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-256185-          },
research/plan-spec.json:256186:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-256187-          "statement": "Let $Q\\in\\{2,3,4\\}$, $L\\geq1$, $\\delta:=\\sqrt Q$, and let $q\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\}$ satisfy $q+q^{-1}=\\delta$. Use the $2L-1$ open-chain operators $e_i$ defined for this Potts-clock chain, and put $g_i:=qI-e_i$ for $1\\leq i\\leq2L-1$. Then $u_i\\mapsto e_i$ represents the rank-$2L$ Temperley-Lieb algebra $P_{2L}(\\mathbb C,\\delta)$, and\n$$(g_i-qI)(g_i+q^{-1}I)=0,\\qquad g_ig_{i+1}g_i=g_{i+1}g_ig_{i+1},\\qquad g_ig_j=g_jg_i\\quad(|i-j|>1).$$\nThese are the type-A Hecke relations in the normalized generator convention after the coefficient specialization $v\\mapsto q^{-1}$. The specified clock-shift model selects $q=e^{i\\pi/4},e^{i\\pi/6},1$ for $Q=2,3,4$, respectively. At $Q=4$, $q=1$ and the same operators $g_i=I-e_i$ satisfy the symmetric-group Coxeter relations, so they define an action of $S_{2L}$. No faithfulness, semisimplicity, or unitarity is asserted.",
research/plan-spec.json-256188-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-256227-            "thm-nrqmx-spin-half-temperley-lieb": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-256228-          },
research/plan-spec.json:256229:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-256230-          "statement": "Let $N\\geq1$ and let $\\mathcal H_N=(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes N}$ have the standard tensor-product Hermitian inner product, linear in its first argument, with $|0\\rangle,|1\\rangle$ orthonormal on each factor. For $1\\leq i<N$, let $s_i$ be the swap of tensor factors $i,i+1$, let $|\\omega\\rangle=(|01\\rangle-|10\\rangle)/\\sqrt2$, and let $P_i=I^{\\otimes(i-1)}\\otimes|\\omega\\rangle\\langle\\omega|\\otimes I^{\\otimes(N-i-1)}$ be the projection onto this singlet on those two factors. Put $e_i:=I-s_i$. Then these are the loop-weight-two Temperley-Lieb generators. In the Hecke normalization $g_i(q):=qI-e_i$, at $q=1$ one has $g_i(1)=s_i$. For arbitrary real coefficients $\\mathcal J_i$, the finite exchange sum\n$$X_N(\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal J}):=\\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\\mathcal J_i s_i$$\nsatisfies\n$$X_N(\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal J})=\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\\mathcal J_i\\right)I-\\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\\mathcal J_i e_i.$$\nThe equality $g_i(1)=s_i$ is internal to this spin-half representation; it does not identify its state space with the distinct $Q=4$ Potts representation.",
research/plan-spec.json-256231-          "provenance": {
--
research/plan-spec.json-256279-            "cor-exponential-is-a-bijection-onto-positive-reals": "mathematical-premise"
research/plan-spec.json-256280-          },
research/plan-spec.json:256281:          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
research/plan-spec.json-256282-          "statement": "Fix $Q\\in\\{2,3,4\\}$ and the two-site open chain $L=2$. Let $\\kappa,\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$ with $\\kappa\\neq0$ and finite $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$, and set $H=-\\kappa e_1-\\lambda e_2=-\\sqrt Q(\\kappa P_1+\\lambda D_{12})$. A classical diagonal replacement here means a density matrix diagonal in the computational basis $|ab\\rangle$. The exact finite Gibbs density $\\rho_\\beta$ of this matrix is not diagonal in that basis. Moreover $P_1,D_{12}$ are nontrivial projections with spectrum $\\{0,1\\}$, satisfy $P_1D_{12}P_1=Q^{-1}P_1$, and do not commute.",
research/plan-spec.json-256283-          "provenance": {
