research/plan-spec.json-260250-          "statement": "Take two sectors with probabilities $p_1,p_2>0$ and $p_1+p_2=1$. Let $H_1,H_2$ be nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product spaces, choose density matrices $\\rho_1,\\rho_2$ on them, and choose $q_1,q_2>0$ with $q_1+q_2=1$ and faithful reference density matrices $\\sigma_1,\\sigma_2$ on the same spaces. Let the first ancillary space be one-dimensional with $\\chi_1=[1]$, and let the second be $\\mathbb C^d$ for an integer $d\\ge1$, with $\\chi_2=I_d/d$. The encoded state has entropy\n\n$$s(\\rho_A)=H(p_1,p_2)+p_1s(\\rho_1)+p_2s(\\rho_2)+p_2\\log d,$$\n\nwhere $H(p_1,p_2):=-p_1\\log p_1-p_2\\log p_2$ is the sector-probability entropy in nats. The sector-probability contribution is $H(p_1,p_2)$ and the ancillary contribution is $p_2\\log d$; when $d=1$, the ancillary contribution is zero. This is an exact finite matrix example and asserts no literal black-hole area law.",
research/plan-spec.json-260251-          "provenance": {
