research/plan-spec.json-260608-          "statement": "For a finite fusion transfer count model, let $e_0\\in\\mathbb R^I$ be the coordinate vector equal to $1$ at label $0$ and $0$ elsewhere, and define $v_n:=N^n e_0$. Then $v_0=e_0$, $v_{n+1}=Nv_n$, and the number of length-$n$ paths from $0$ to a label $a$ is $(v_n)_a=(N^n)_{a0}$. Whenever $D_n>0$, the operator $\\rho_n=D_n^{-1}I_{\\mathbb C^{D_n}}$ is a density matrix and has von Neumann entropy $s(\\rho_n)=\\log D_n$ in nats. For the supplied two-label matrix $N=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&1\\end{pmatrix}$, with labels ordered $0,1$, one has $D_0=1$, $D_1=0$, $D_2=1$, and $D_{n+2}=D_{n+1}+D_n$ for every $n\\geq0$.",
