research/plan-spec.json-260723-          "statement": "Under the finite Hilbert representation data, let $r:=\\operatorname{rank}P>0$ and $\\rho:=P/r$. An **orthogonal projection** on $H$ means a complex-linear endomorphism $Q$ satisfying $Q^2=Q$ and $\\langle Qx,y\\rangle=\\langle x,Qy\\rangle$ for all $x,y\\in H$. Then $P$ is an orthogonal projection, $\\rho$ is a density matrix with eigenvalue $1/r$ of multiplicity $r$ and eigenvalue $0$ on $\\ker P$, and its entropy is $s(\\rho)=\\log r$ in nats. Under the published closure convention, the unnormalized diagrammatic closure trace of the algebraic Jones-Wenzl element is $\\operatorname{Tr}_n(p_n)=[n+1]_\\delta$. The proposition records this separately from the ordinary Hilbert-space trace $\\operatorname{tr}_H(P)=r$ and does not assert the two values agree. A sufficient additional hypothesis for equality on this element is that the representation preserve these traces, $\\operatorname{tr}_H(\\pi(\\Phi_n^{-1}(X)))=\\operatorname{Tr}_n(X)$ for every $X\\in\\mathrm{TL}_n(\\mathbb C,\\delta)$.\n\n",
research/plan-spec.json-260724-          "provenance": {
