research/plan-spec.json-260791-          "statement": "For the two-label matrix $N=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&1\\end{pmatrix}$ in the finite fusion count model, $D_4=2$. Choose a positive scalar $a$ independently of $N$ and set $A_4:=4a$. The ratio between the model entropy $\\log D_4$ and this separately assigned scalar is $\\log2/(4a)$, and it changes when $a$ is replaced by $2a$ although $N$ and $D_4$ are unchanged. Thus the finite count alone does not determine a proportionality coefficient between its entropy and an independently assigned area-like scalar. The scalar $A_4$ is formal data in this mathematical example; no geometrical area, physical entropy, or gravitational law is asserted.",
